"moringa_masoor_dal_recipe_drumstick_leaves_dal": { title: "Moringa Masoor Dal Recipe - Drumstick Leaves Dal", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 Dry Red Chilli","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 cup Pink Masoor Dal (Split)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","200 grams Drumstick Leaves (Moringa/Murungai Keerai) - cleaned chopped","1 Green Chilli - slit","1 tablespoon Ghee","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1 Lemon - juice extracted","1 inch Ginger - finely chopped","2 teaspoons Coriander Powder (Dhania)"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,4140,973,48,464], steps: ["To prepare the Methi Masoor Dal Recipe, first wash and soak the masoor dal in 3 cups of water for at least 30 minutes","While the dal is soaked clean, wash and pat dry the fenugreek leaves.Next, finely chop the drumstick leaves","Heat a teaspoon of oil in a wok or a kadai and add the chopped drumstick leaves into the wok","Sprinkle some salt, cover the pan and cook the Moringa leaves until soft and tender.It takes about 2 to 3 minutes and no","Once done, turn off the heat and keep the cooked moringa leaves aside.In the next step, cook the masoor dal with the spi","Heat ghee in a pressure cooker over medium heat","Close the lid of the pressure cooker and put the weight on.Cook masoor dal for 3 whistles","After a couple of whistles, turn the heat to low and simmer the dal for about 5 minutes ✅"] },
