"rajasthani_gatte_ki_sabzi_recipe_with_onion_garlic": { title: "Rajasthani Gatte Ki Sabzi Recipe With Onion & Garlic", serves: "3", time: "70 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","3 Cloves (Laung)","2 cups Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","4 cloves Garlic","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","Salt - to taste","1 Bay leaf (tej patta) - torn","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","4 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","1/4 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 Onion - finely chopped","1 cup Gram flour (besan)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,2314,4140,973,4142,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Rajasthani Gatte Ki Sabzi Recipe we will first make the gatte.In a large mixing bowl, combine all th","Add a few teaspoons of water at a time and knead to make a firm dough","Knead well for about 5 minutes to make a very soft melt in the mouth gatta","If you add more water and it does not shape into a dough, then you will have to add more gram flour and knead it well.Ro","The next step is to cook the gattas in boiling water.In a large saucepan boil water until it comes to a brisk boil","Once the water comes to a brisk boil, add the gattas into the water and boil until they comes floating to the top","Once they come floating to the top, boil for another 3 to 4 minutes","Drain the gattas and keep it aside, till we get the Kadhi ready.To make the kadhi, in a mixing bowl, combine the yogurt,"] },
"bengali_aloo_potol_er_dalna_recipe_a_traditional_v": { title: "Bengali Aloo Potol er Dalna Recipe - A Traditional Vegetable Side Dish", serves: "3", time: "65 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Kashmiri Red Chilli Powder","1 Dry Red Chilli","1 teaspoon Sugar","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 inch Ginger - grated","1 Tomato - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2314,973,1844,473], steps: ["To begin making the Bengali Aloo Potol er Dalna Recipe, first prep all the ingredients, get them together and keep ready","In the traditional method, you would cook both the aloo and potol separately and then make the masala and add to it","The following method, is a healthy way of cooking the recipe and uses much less oil.Heat a teaspoon of oil in the pressu","Add the cumin seeds, dry red chilies, the cinnamon, cloves, cardamom and saute till the aromas are released","Add the chopped tomatoes and saute till the tomatoes soften.Once the tomatoes soften, add the turmeric powder, chili pow","once the pressure is released, open the pressure cooker the the Aloo Potol er Dalna should be done","If the gravy is too watery, simmer and allow the water to evaporate and let the gravy thicken","Once done, check the salt and spices and adjust to suit your taste ✅"] },
"egg_sholay_kebab_recipe": { title: "Egg Sholay Kebab Recipe", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 tablespoon Gram flour (besan)","1 teaspoon Green Chilli - paste","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","6 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","5 Whole Eggs - hard boiled","3 tablespoons All Purpose Flour (Maida)","2 inch Ginger - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Sambar Powder","3 sprig Curry leaves"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,4148,920,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Egg Sholay Kebab Recipe, keep the hard boiled eggs ready","Cut them into half and set aside","To make the batter for the Egg Sholay In a mixing bowl, combine the besan and rice flour along with the maida","Once the oil is well heated, reduce the flame to medium-low","Now dunk the boiled eggs into the batter and gradually lower the well coated egg into the hot oil","Deep fry on medium flame, until the Egg Sholay Kebab are crisp and deep brown in colour","Drain the Egg Sholay Kebab on an absorbent paper ✅"] },
