"paka_kela_ki_sabzi_recipe_paka_kela_nu_shaak_gujar": { title: "Paka Kela Ki Sabzi Recipe | Paka Kela nu Shaak | Gujarati Jain Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/4 cup Gram flour (besan)","3 cups Ripe Bananas - cubed","2 teaspoons Sunflower Oil","Salt - to taste","1/4 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1/4 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1 sprig Curry leaves - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [2307,2308,973,15,920,27,2300,2301], steps: ["Turn off heat and transfer to a serving dish.Serve Paka Kela Ki Sabzi along with of Phulka, Gujarati Dal and a bowl of d","Note: The Paka Kela Ki Sabzi has to be prepared just a few minutes before you are ready to serve your meal","When it stays for a longer time, the bananas tend  to lose their texture and the dish can get too soggy ✅"] },
"chocolate_tart_recipe": { title: "Chocolate Tart Recipe", serves: "3", time: "180 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1/4 teaspoon Salt","300 grams Dark chocolate - chopped (I used bournville)","3/4 cup Butter (unsalted) - cold and cut into pea size pieces","1/2 cup Milk","2 tablespoons Sugar","2 cups All Purpose Flour (Maida) - plus more for dusting","2 Whole Eggs - at room temperature","2 tablespoons Water - temperature to be at ice cold plus more if needed","1 cup Heavy whipping cream - (I used amul cream in india)","3 tablespoons Sugar"], product_ids: [2314,4141,4144,4148,2300,2302], steps: ["We begin making the Chocolate Tart Recipe by following the below procedures:Method for making the tart crustIn a large m","Add the butter and mix the butter into the flour with your fingers until the mixture resembles coarse crumbs","Add in a tablespoon of ice water at a time and knead to bring the flour together.Knead to form a firm dough that is firm","Make sure you only add a tablespoon of water at a time, as the warmth of your hand will help bring the flour together to","Wrap the pastry crust dough in cling wrap and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes.After 30 minutes, roll out the pastry ","Roll it out to make a circle of 12 inch diameter that is about 1/4 inch thick","Lift the dough carefully from the floured surface and place it in a 9 inch tart pan with a removable base.Press the doug","It is important to press the dough evenly into every nook and corner of the pan's ring ✅"] },
"navrang_dal_recipe_navrang_dal_recipe": { title: "Navrang dal recipe - Navrang Dal (Recipe)", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoons White Urad Dal","2 tablespoons Kali Urad Dal","1 tablespoon arhar dal - soaked for 20 minutes","1 onion - finely chopped","1 tablespoon ginger garlic paste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli Powder","1 teaspoon cumin seeds","2 Tablespoons Kabuli Chana","1/4 Cup yellow moong dal - soaked for 20 minutes","2 tablespoons Green Moong Dal","2 tablespoons Ghee","salt - as per taste"], product_ids: [545,930,929,2307,2308,2314,4140,973], steps: ["To make Navrang dal, first soak all the lentils overnight","Soak pili moong dal and arhar dal for 20 minutes","Put the lentils in the pressure cooker in the morning and cook till 3 years come","After the cooker cools, mash the pour and keep it aside","Now heat oil in a pan and add ghee to it","After that add cinnamon, cumin and let it cook for 15 seconds","After 15 seconds, add onion and let it cook till it turns light brown","Now add garlic ginger paste and let it cook for 2 minutes ✅"] },
"green_moong_dal_sundal_recipe_green_moong_dal_sund": { title: "Green Moong Dal Sundal Recipe - Green Moong Dal Sundal Recipe", serves: "3", time: "440 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 tsp rye","2 sprig coriander - chopped","2 sprig curry leaves","1 tbsp lemon juice","1/4 tsp asafoetida","1 tsp sesame oil","1 Cup sprouted moong","1 tsp cumin","salt - as per taste","2 green chillies - chopped","2 tbsp coconut - tighten"], product_ids: [930,2307,9,973,48,503,920,2301], steps: ["To make green moong dal sundal recipe, first of all sprout green moons or you can also use sprouted green moong from the","Now heat oil in a pan","Add mustard seeds and let it splutter","Add the cumin seeds, asafoetida, green chillies and curry leaves to it after the rai crackles","After the curry leaves crackle, add sprouted green moong, salt, mix, cover the pan and cook for 3 to 4 minutes","Open the pan and add grated coconut, lemon juice, green coriander and mix","Turn off the gas and serve","Serve green moong dal sundal recipe with tomato rasam, chow chow thoran, rice and curry leaves for dinner ✅"] },
"chow_chow_sambar_recipe_chow_chow_sambar": { title: "Chow Chow Sambar Recipe - Chow-Chow Sambar", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["2 cups chow chow - chop","30 grams tamarind - soaked in 1 cup water","1 onion - thinly sliced","4 sprigs of coriander - chopped","1 red chili","2 tomatoes - chopped","1 cup arhar dal","1 teaspoon sesame oil - or any oil","1 teaspoon mustard","1 tablespoon sambar powder","1/4 teaspoon asafoetida","salt - as per taste"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2311,973,2300,503], steps: ["To make chow chow sambar, first put 2 cups water, turmeric powder, salt along with lentils in a pressure cooker and cook","After the lentils are cooked, mash the lentils well and keep them aside","Heat the oil in a pan","Add onions and cook till they become soft","Now add tomatoes and chow chow","Cook until 3/4 of the chow is cooked","Bitch kept shaking in between","Now add tamarind water, sambar powder, salt and cook it until the chow is cooked well ✅"] },
"tamil_nadu_style_white_paniyaram_recipe_semi_sweet": { title: "Tamil Nadu Style White Paniyaram Recipe - Semi Sweet Rice & Dal Printe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["Sunflower Oil - for deep frying","1 tablespoon Sugar","Salt - to taste","1/4 cup Milk","1 cup Rice - soaked for 2 hours","2 tablespoon Black Urad Dal (Whole) - soaked for 2 hours"], product_ids: [2308,2314,4141,503,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Tamil Nadu Style Vellai Paniyaram Recipe, wash and soak rice and urad dal in water for 2 hours.Grind","Keep the batter as thick as possible.Add sugar and salt to the batter, and let it rest for another hour.Heat oil in a Ka","Add milk to make it watery at this stage","The consistency should be more watery than a dosa batter.Drop one tablespoon full of batter into the Kadai","It will rise and puff up","Once the Vellai paniyaram is cooked on one side, flip it and let it fry for a couple of seconds","Transfer Vellai Paniyaram on a kitchen towel","Pat the Vellai Paniyaram with an oil absorbent paper to remove excess oil and serve.Serve Vellai Paniyaram spicy Tangy T"] },
