"broccoli_soup_recipe_for_babies_toddlers_above_7_m": { title: "Broccoli Soup Recipe - For Babies/Toddlers above 7 months", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🍵 Soup", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Butter (unsalted)","Salt - a pinch","3 Badam (Almond) - soaked in hot water","1 cup Broccoli - 10 florets approximately","Black pepper powder - a pinch"], product_ids: [2307,4144,1843,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Broccoli Soup, we begin by washing the broccoli florets thoroughly","Once the Broccoli is washed, add this to a pressure cooker with 1/4 cup of water and a pinch of salt","Close the lid and pressure cook for 1 whistle","Add the cooled Broccoli florets along with the water that it was cooked in and the almonds into a mixer and blend until ","Place a pan on low heat and add half a teaspoon of butter to the pan","Once the butter melts, add the blended broccoli to the pan and sprinkle a pinch of pepper.Stir well until all the ingred","Let the broccoli soup for the baby stay on low heat for 2-3 minutes, turn off the heat","Serve this Broccoli soup to you baby or toddler who is over 7 months for lunch or dinner ✅"] },
"karnataka_special_huli_tovve_recipe": { title: "Karnataka Special Huli Tovve Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["Curry leaves - as required","Salt - to taste","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1 cup Mixed vegetables - (french beans","Asafoetida (hing) - A pinch","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","6 Dry Red Chillies","1/4 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1/4 cup Raw Peanuts (Moongphali)","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 tablespoon Jaggery","1 tablespoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)"], product_ids: [2307,2308,9,2314,460,973,503,920], steps: ["To begin with Huli Tovve, wash and soak the toor dal till you prepare your vegetables.Wash and cut the vegetables","Pressure cook Toor dal, mixed vegetables and peanuts till they the cooker releases 3-4 whistles.The next step is to prep","Dry roast urad dal, chana dal, cinnamon and red chilli separately till they turn light gold","Add coconut to this and grind all of this into a smooth paste.Remove the lid after the cooker cools down","Add the ground paste to this and 2 cups of water, salt and jaggery and boil","Boil till the hulitovve thickens on high flame.For tempering, heat the oil in a tadka pan","Add mustard seeds and let it crackle","Add red chilly and curry leaves ✅"] },
"garlic_tikki_recipe": { title: "Garlic Tikki Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Paneer (Homemade Cottage Cheese) - grated","10 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","Salt - to taste","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","7 Potatoes (Aloo) - boiled","10 Cashew nuts - finely chopped","1 Onion - finely chopped","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","1/4 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 tablespoon Corn flour","Sunflower Oil - for frying"], product_ids: [930,2307,973,4145,1842,2300,4152,473], steps: ["To begin making Lehsuni Aloo Tikki Recipe, wash and boil the potatoes in enough water","Once cooked, peel the skin and keep aside","You can also pressure cook the potatoes for 2 whistles and allow the pressure to release naturally","Peel the skin and keep aside","To prepare the outer layer of the Lehsuni Aloo Tikki, in a large bowl add in the boiled potatoes and mash them well","Add cornflour, season with salt and mix well","Add a spoonful of the paneer filling into the potato mix, seal it from all sides ✅"] },
"baked_fish_crisps_recipe_fish_fry_in_oven": { title: "Baked Fish Crisps Recipe (Fish Fry In Oven)", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Water","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Sunflower Oil - optional","2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","10 Fish - pieces","5 teaspoon Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [2307,973,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Baked Fish Crisps Recipe, clean the fish and in a large vessel add in the ingredients mentioned in t","Meanwhile line your baking tray with Parchment paper","Preheat the oven at 180 Deg c for about 10 mins","Arranged the marinated fish pieces in the lined baking tray and using grill mode grill it for 7 mins","After 7 mins flip the fish and then grill for another 7 mins","Now that the colour of the fish would have slightly turned dark","Flip the side of the fish once again and brush it with oil if required","And grill for another 5 mins.Once done flip the fish once again and brush with little oil or sprinkle little oil and gri"] },
"left_over_vadai_upma_recipe": { title: "Left Over Vadai Upma Recipe", serves: "3", time: "15 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1 Dry Red Chilli","Sunflower Oil - as required","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","Salt - to taste","6 Medu vada","1 tablespoon Ginger - finely chopped","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","1 Onion - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","1 sprig Curry leaves","1 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves","1 pinch Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,2300,503,920,476], steps: ["To begin making the Left Over Vadai Upma recipe, you can either use ready made medu vadas or make them at home b y follo","Break the vadas with your hands and make it appear like crumbs","Heat a wok/kadhai on medium flame, add the oil, once the oil is hot, add hing, mustard seeds, bengal gram dal, red chill","Add green chillies, onions and let it fry for a minute","Add onion, salt, turmeric and let it cook well.Add curry leaves and let it cook for a minute","Add the crumbled vadai and mix well","Let it cook well for 2 to 3 minutes","Garnish with coriander leaves.Serve Left Over Vadai Upma with South Indian Coconut Chutney for breakfast and a cup of Be"] },
