"gur_paare_recipe_a_traditional_punjabi_wedding_swe": { title: "Gur Paare Recipe (A traditional Punjabi Wedding Sweet)", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["500 grams All Purpose Flour (Maida)","1/4 cup Ghee","250 grams Jaggery","Sunflower Oil - for deep frying","1 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)"], product_ids: [2307,2314,4140,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Gur Paare Recipe in a large mixing bowl add the maida and the melted ghee.Keep mixing the flour and ","At this point add teaspoons of water at a time and knead it to make a firm dough.Divide the dough in four parts and roll","Cut them into vertical strips and then into 2-3 inch long strips","Repeat for rest of the dough portions.In a kadai, heat oil for deep frying on medium heat","Once the oil is hot, add the cut dough strips and fry until slightly brown and crisp","Do make sure to fry on medium heat so it gets crisp evenly.Drain them on a kitchen towel and allow them to cool a bit.In","On a slow flame allow it to melt, stirring continuously all the time.Cook till you attain the consistency where you add ","Turn off the heat and immediately add the fried strips to the jaggery syrup ✅"] },
