"malpua_recipe_with_rabri_a_spiced_indian_pancake_w": { title: "Malpua Recipe with Rabri (A Spiced Indian Pancake with Milk Pudding)", serves: "3", time: "65 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["3 to 4 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds - crushed","1 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)","1/2 cup Sugar","3 tablespoons Khoya (Mawa) - crumbled","1 tablespoon Caster Sugar","3 tablespoon Milk Powder","1/4 cup Water","2 - 3 Saffron strands","Lemon juice - of 1/2 lemon","1 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf) - crushed","1/4 teaspoon Baking soda","Ghee - for frying the malpua"], product_ids: [2307,2314,4140,4141,4142,48,2300], steps: ["To begin making Malpua Recipe, first prepare the batter","To do this, in a mixing bowl mix stir together the flour, sugar, milk powder, crushed cardamom pods and fennel seeds.Now","Stir and mix well to combine.Using a little water at a time, mix continuously until the batter forms a thick flowing con","It should flow like dosa batter","Set it aside so the batter can rest for 30 minutes.Meanwhile prepare the sugar syrup in which you will soak the malpua","To do this, add sugar and water in a heavy bottom saucepan","Set it on a low heat and let it simmer until the sugar has melted completely.Once sugar is dissolved add the lemon juice","Stir once to combine ✅"] },
