"dum_pukht_gosht_recipe_slow_cooked_mutton_curry": { title: "Dum Pukht Gosht Recipe - Slow Cooked Mutton Curry", serves: "3", time: "75 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 Onion - sliced","1-1/2 cups Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","8 cloves Garlic","1 teaspoon Black pepper corns","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/4 cup Coriander (Dhania) Leaves","Ghee - for cooking","Water - for kneading","500 grams Mutton","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 teaspoon Cumin (Jeera) seeds","4 Green Chillies"], product_ids: [930,2307,2314,4140,973,4142,1842,2300], steps: ["To begin making Dum Pukht Gosht we will first prepare the ingredients required for marinating the mutton","Turn off the heat and let it cool.Once cooled add the caramelized onions and the whole spices to a mixer grinder","Add the garlic, ginger, green chillies and half the curd and grind to a smooth paste","Marinate the mutton with the above ground spice curd and onion mixture","While the mutton is marinating knead the dough that you need to seal the vessel in which you are going to cook the gosht","This will take about 10 minutes","Add one glass of water and bring the Mutton gosht to a boil.Cover the handi with a lid and seal it with the wheat dough ","Give it a stir and adjust the salt accordingly ✅"] },
"idli_manchurian_recipe_with_oriental_twist": { title: "Idli Manchurian Recipe With Oriental Twist", serves: "3", time: "130 min", category: "🥡 Indo-Chinese", all_ingredients: ["5 Idli","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","1-2 tablespoons Dried oregano","1 Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum)","1-2 teaspoons Spring Onion Greens - chopped","2 Green Chillies - (adjust)","1 teaspoon Ginger - grated","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 Onion","2 Soy sauce"], product_ids: [930,2307,2311,973,1840,2300,2301,476], steps: ["To prepare Idli Manchurian Recipe With Oriental Twist, get all the ingredients ready along with leftover idlis","Or make idlis from idli batter in idli steamer and keep aside for 1-2 hours or more","Cut each idli into 6-7 pieces.Heat a shallow fry pan and add a teaspoon of oil and spread evenly.Place 6-8 pieces of idl","This is one way of making crunchy idli pieces","I prefer making the crispy idli pieces this way","The other way (easier way) is shallow fry whole idlis until they turn light brown.Then cut these idlis into 6-7 pieces","Now, heat another pan, with a wide base","Add the remaining oil ✅"] },
