"palak_onion_kadhi_pakora_recipe": { title: "Palak Onion Kadhi Pakora Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["50 grams Spinach - finely chopped","1 Onion - chopped","1 Green Chilli - chopped","1 tablespoon Ghee","1 cup Hung Curd (Greek Yogurt)","Sunflower Oil - as required","Salt - to taste","1/4 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1/2 teaspoon Enos fruit salt","2-1/2 cups Lukewarm Water","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,2314,4140,973,4142,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Palak Onion Kadhi Pakora Recipe, we will make the pakoras first","*Method for Pakora'sCombine all the ingredients for the palak pakora in a large bowl","Add very little water to make a thick batter.Heat the kuzhi paniyaram pan on medium heat; add a teaspoon of oil into eac","Cover the pan and steam cook the pakora's until you notice the top has steamed.Once the top has steamed, flip them over ","Continue to cook on medium heat until the pakoras has cooked through from the inside and have a golden brown color","Proceed the same way with the remaining pakora batter and keep them aside.*Method for the Punjabi KadhiWhisk the yogurt,","Add the water and whisk more until well blended","Place the kadhi in a saucepan, on medium high heat and allow it to come to a brisk boil.Keep whisking it continuously wh"] },
"dry_navratan_korma_recipe_in_hindi": { title: "Dry Navratan Korma (Recipe In Hindi)", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup pomegranate","2 bay leaves","2 onions - chopped","2 tomatoes - puree","1/2 tablespoon garam masala powder","cashews - some","1 cabbage - cut into small pieces","1/2 cup green chili","2 carrots - finely chopped","1 cinnamon","1 Inch ginger - chopped","1 teaspoon celery"], product_ids: [0,2307,8,15,24,545,930,1840], steps: ["To make Navratan Korma (dry), first of all prepare the ingredients","Now heat oil in a pan and add pieces of paneer to it","Fry it well and drain it to soak more oil on a tissue","Add some more oil and add all the spices","After 10 seconds, add onion and cook till it becomes soft","After the onion is soft, add ginger garlic paste and green chillies","Cook it for 2 to 3 minutes","Now add tomato puree and cook for 3 to 5 minutes ✅"] },
"madurai_spicy_tomato_chutney_recipe": { title: "Madurai Spicy Tomato Chutney Recipe", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 tsp rye","3 tsp sesame oil","2 sprig curry leaves","1/2 tsp sugar","5 dry red chillies","2 tomatoes","salt - as per taste","1/4 cup water","2 tsp tamarind Paste","2 tsp urad dal","2 onions"], product_ids: [545,2308,2311,2314,973,503,920,476], steps: ["To make Madurai Tomato Chutney Recipe, first cut the onion tomatoes and keep them separately","Now heat oil in a pan","Add dry red chillies, onions, tomatoes and cook for 5 minutes","Turn off the gas and allow it to cool","Pour this mixture into the mixer grinder with 2 tablespoons of water and grind it","Now heat sesame oil in a pan","Add mustard seeds and let it splutter","Now add urad dal, curry leaves and cook the urad dal till it becomes golden brown ✅"] },
"baked_cauliflower_samosa_recipe": { title: "Baked Cauliflower Samosa Recipe", serves: "3", time: "85 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["2 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1 Dry Red Chilli","1 tablespoon Sugar","1 teaspoon Kasuri Methi (Dried Fenugreek Leaves)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","5 Green Chillies","1 tablespoon Ginger - grated","1 cup Cauliflower (gobi) - small florets","Water - as needed","1 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)","1/2 teaspoon Salt"], product_ids: [929,2307,2314,973,465,503,473,2300], steps: ["To begin making Baked Cauliflower Samosa Recipe, prepare all the ingredients and start with making the dough.In a bowl, ","Keep mixing with hand  until the dough becomes crumbly enough to take a shape.Add water and make a medium tight dough, a","Mix it properly then let it cook on low heat","Stir occasionally until vegetables are well cooked","Add kasuri methi and let it cool before proceeding to stuffing it.Making SamosasPreheat oven into 350 F(180 C).Divide do","with a rolling pin roll each dough in a round shape to medium thickness then cut them in the middle","Take one portion of the flattened dough and shape like a cone overlapping the flat side together","Now put 1 and 1/2 tsp of stuffing inside the samosa cone and seal the edges with brushing water on the edges ✅"] },
"tomato_basil_chicken_recipe": { title: "Tomato Basil Chicken Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1/4 cup Basil leaves - fresh leaves","2 teaspoons Extra Virgin Olive Oil","2 teaspoons Mixed Herbs (Dried)","1 tablespoon Mixed Herbs (Dried)","2 Chicken breasts","10 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","Salt - to taste","Sugar - to taste","1 sprig Basil leaves - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 tablespoons Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1 Onion - finely chopped"], product_ids: [545,2303,2307,2314,973,48,2300,476], steps: ["To begin making the Tomato Basil Chicken Recipe, wash and thoroughly clean the chicken breasts","Into the bowl add the chicken, add mixed herbs, lemon juice, olive oil and salt","Heat a skillet on medium-high heat to pan sear the chicken pieces","Next add the torn basil leaves, tomato puree, herbs, red chilli powder, salt and sugar","Bring the tomato basil sauce to a brisk boil","After a few minutes, add the grilled chicken breasts into the tomato basil sauce ✅"] },
