"keri_na_gotla_nu_shaak_recipe_gujarati_style_ripe": { title: "Keri Na Gotla Nu Shaak Recipe - Gujarati Style Ripe Mango Curry", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["3 Mango (Ripe)","1/2 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 Dry Red Chilli","Salt - to taste","1/2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1/2 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 tablespoons Jaggery - adjust as per sourness of mango","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 1/2 tablespoons Gram flour (besan)","1 teaspoon Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [1,930,2307,2308,2314,973,503,920], steps: ["To begin making the Keri Na Gotla Nu Shaak Recipe, we need to soften the whole mangoes by rolling it in between your pal","To this bowl, add besan and fold it in gently","Make sure that there should be any no lumps in the mixture","Next add 3/4 cup of water, along with the red chili powder, roasted cumin powder, coriander powder, jaggery and salt.Tra","Once the Keri Na Gotla Nu Shaak gets a single boil, reduce the flame, and let it simmer for 10 minutes and turn off the ","Heat oil in a tadka pan on medium flame, add mustard seeds, curry leaves and allow them to crackle","Next add the urad dal, and allow it to turn into a lovely golden brown colour, after which you need to add turmeric powd","Turn off the flame ✅"] },
