"tomato_kurma_recipe_thakkali_kurma_for_biryani_par": { title: "Tomato Kurma Recipe - Thakkali Kurma For Biryani & Parotta", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["3 Green Chillies","3 tablespoons Fresh coconut - grated","4 Tomatoes - finely chopped","Salt - as per your taste","1 tablespoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)","1 tablespoon Water","2 Star anise","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 tablespoons Sambar Powder","2 Onions - finely chopped","2 teaspoons Ghee"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,9,2314,4140,973,2300], steps: ["To begin making Tomato Kurma Recipe, we will first grind all the ingredients needs for the Kurma paste.In a mixer combin","Grind the ingredients until you get a smooth paste","Keep aside for later.Next, place a heavy bottomed pan on medium heat and add 2 teaspoons of ghee","Once the ghee is warm, add cumin seeds and allow it to sizzle.When the cumin seeds are sizzling, add the star anise, cin","Next, add the chopped tomatoes along with sambar powder and saute until the tomatoes are soft and mushy","Once the tomatoes are mushy, add the ground kurma paste, salt to taste and simmer the flame to low","Add 1/4 cup water, stir and close the lid of the pan","Let the tomato kurma simmer for 5 minutes ✅"] },
