"nellor_kathirikai_nellor_brinjal_fry_recipe": { title: "Nellor Kathirikai - Nellor Brinjal Fry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["4 Dry Red Chillies","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","10 Small Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant) - quartered and soaked in salt water","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","1 teaspoon Sesame (Gingelly) Oil","Salt - to taste","1/2 cup Water","2 sprig Curry leaves - torn","1/4 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1 tablespoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 Onion - thinly sliced"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,9,973,4148,469,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Nellor Brinjal Fry Recipe, prepare all the ingredients and keep them ready.Soak the cut brinjal in s","Heat oil in a pan over medium heat; add the mustard seeds and curry leaves and allow the mustard seeds to crackle.Drain ","Stir to combine and cover the pan and cook the brinjal until the brinjal is roasted and cooked","Keep this aside.To make the Nellor Masala, in a pan add the chana dal, coriander seeds and red chillies","Roast them well until the dal has turned golden brown","Cover the pan and simmer for 5 minutes and turn off the heat.Check the salt and chillies and adjust to taste accordingly","Once done, transfer the Nellor Brinjal Fry to a serving bowl and serve hot.Serve the Nellor Brinjal Fry Recipe along wit"] },
"jeera_miri_kolambi_recipe_cumin_black_pepper_prawn": { title: "Jeera Miri Kolambi Recipe - Cumin & Black Pepper Prawns", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["2 cloves Garlic","Salt - to taste","10 Whole Black Peppercorns","1 Tomato - finely chopped","4 tablespoons Sunflower Oil","1 inch Ginger","1 Onion - finely chopped","2 Dry Red Chillies","2 tablespoons Coriander (Dhania) Leaves","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","300 grams Prawns - shelled and deveined","5 Curry leaves"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,973,1842,2300,920,476], steps: ["Make a smooth spice paste.Marinade the prawns with the paste and add some salt","Keep aside.Heat the oil in a kadai","On a medium high heat, add the curry leaves and the onions","Stir occasionally.When the onions are caramelised, add the tomato paste or chopped tomato","Cook on medium heat till the tomatoes are mushy and the onions and tomatoes have come together.Add the prawns along with","Add about 1/4 cup of water and cook on high heat till the prawns are done and all the water has evaporated ✅"] },
"savory_waffles_with_roasted_peppers_in_sun_dried_t": { title: "Savory Waffles With Roasted Peppers In Sun Dried Tomato Pesto Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1/2 Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - diced","2 teaspoons Baking powder","1 Whole Egg","2 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","2 tablespoons Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1 sprig Basil leaves - roughly chopped","Salt - to taste","50 grams Sun Dried Tomatoes - drain the excess oil","2 tablespoons Pickled Jalapenos - sliced","1/4 cup Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [545,2303,2307,2314,973,4141,1840,4145], steps: ["Switch to high heat and pan fry them for 2-3 minutes.Finally add in the sundried tomato pesto and give it a good stir","Turn off the flame.For the savoury wafflesPreheat waffle iron","Beat eggs in large bowl with hand beater until fluffy","Beat in milk, vegetable oil, sugar, baking powder, pepper, oregano and salt, just until smooth","Finally add in the flour and stir to combine well, until it is smooth with no lumpsGrease the waffle iron pan with oil","Pour mix on to hot waffle iron","Cook until golden brown","To assemble, place the waffles on a plate, top with mixed bell peppers ✅"] },
