"soya_chunks_masala_in_coconut_milk_recipe": { title: "Soya Chunks Masala in Coconut Milk Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon Curry powder","3 cloves Garlic - grated","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 Onion - finely chopped","2 Tomatoes - finely sliced","2 cups Soy Chunks (Nuggets) - boiled and squeezed well","3 Green Chillies - slit"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,9,973,4141,2300,920], steps: ["To begin making the Soya Chunks Masala in Coconut Milk Recipe, get all the ingredients ready.Heat water in a saucepan an","Add the soy chunks into the water and allow it to boil for a couple of minutes until the soy chunks soak in a lot of wat","This will take about 5 minutes","once the soy chunks have soaked in the water and become soft, drain out the water and keep the soy chunks aside.The next","Add the cumin, curry leaves and green chilies and saute them for a few seconds","Add the onions, ginger, garlic and saute until the onions become soft and translucent.Add sliced tomatoes and saute for ","Once the tomatoes soften, add the coriander powder, red chilli powder and turmeric powder, mix well","Cook for half a minute.Add soya chunks and saute in the masala for 2 to 3 minutes ✅"] },
