"karnataka_style_orange_peels_curry_recipe": { title: "Karnataka Style Orange Peels Curry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","2 Orange","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","3 tablespoon Jaggery - adjustable","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","Tamarind - big lemon size","1 Green Chilli - slit","1 Dry Red Chilli - broken","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 teaspoon Rasam Powder","1/4 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)"], product_ids: [929,2307,2308,2311,2314,973,16,48], steps: ["To begin making the Karnataka Style Orange Peels Curry recipe, Peel out 2 oranges","Gently scrape the white region from the orange peel using a spoon","Remove as much as possible as this will reduce the bitterness .Chop the orange peels finely.Soak tamarind in water","After it's soaked well, squeeze out tamarind water and keep aside.Heat oil in a heavy bottomed pan and temper with musta","When it splutters add curry leaves, red chilli powder, green chilli, hing and turmeric powder","Mix and add chopped orange peel","Fry for 4-5 minutes.Later add tamarind water, salt, jaggery, red chilli powder and rasam powder","Add some water and close the lid ✅"] },
