"andhra_style_vegetarian_biryani_with_soya_chunks_r": { title: "Andhra Style Vegetarian Biryani with Soya Chunks Recipe", serves: "3", time: "75 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["1 Mace (Javitri)","1 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","Sunflower Oil - or ghee for cooking","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","4 Cloves (Laung)","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 teaspoon Whole Black Peppercorns","3 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)","2 Tomatoes - chopped","2 cup Basmati rice","1 Bay leaf (tej patta)"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,2314,4140,973,1842,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Andhra Style Vegetarian Biryani, soak the soy chunks in 1/4 cup water and keep it aside.Soak the bas","Ground all the spice mix mentioned in the biryani spice mix to a coarse powder.Heat a pressure cooker with oil","Add bay leaf, cardamom, cinnamon stick, cloves, star anise and mace","Fry the spice for 10 seconds until the aroma is released.Add the chopped onions, ginger garlic paste and green chili","Add the soaked soya chunks as well","Mix well till the masala is mixed.Add 4 cups of water, check for salt and pressure cook for 2 whistle and switch off the","Allow the pressure to release by itself and open the lid and mix the rice well with the masala and serve.Serve the Andhr"] },
