"goan_style_brinjal_bharta_recipe": { title: "Goan Style Brinjal Bharta Recipe", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Tamarind Paste","1 Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant)","Salt - to taste","1 Tamarind - marble sized ball","2 Onions - finely chopped","1/2 cup Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","2 Green Chillies - chopped","2 tablespoon Fresh coconut - grated"], product_ids: [930,2311,9,973,4148,469,476,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Goan Style Brinjal Bharta Recipe, clean the brinjal and make 4 to 5 slits keeping the brinjal intact","Switch off the pan and apply this oil to the brinjal","Once done, put the brinjal in the same pan and cover it with a lid.After 2 minutes, open the lid and turn the brinjal ca","Once it is slightly cooked from the other side, carefully insert the marble sized tamarind ball through one slit and aga","This might take 25 to 35 minutes.Once cooked, it will turn brown and will release water","Let the brinjal remain covered until it cools down.After cooling, peel the brinjal and discard the peel","Mash the pulp and mix it with finely chopped onions and green chillies in a bowl.Add grated coconut, tamarind paste, sal","Once done, add finely chopped coriander leaves, mix well and it is ready to be served.Serve Goan Brinjal Bharta Recipe a"] },
"dahi_sabudana_recipe_savory_tapioca_pearls_seasone": { title: "Dahi Sabudana Recipe (Savory Tapioca Pearls Seasoned with Yogurt)", serves: "3", time: "155 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Sugar","Salt - to taste","1 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt) - fresh","2 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 cup Sabudana (Tapioca Pearls)","2-3 Green Chillies - chopped","1 tablespoon Ghee","2-3 tablespoons Groundnut powder - roasted"], product_ids: [2307,2314,4140,973,13,4142,2300,2302], steps: ["You can also serve Dahi Sabudana on its own or along with a sweet lime pickle ✅"] },
"horsegram_and_foxtail_millet_idli_recipe": { title: "Horsegram And Foxtail Millet Idli Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🌅 Breakfast", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoons Poha (Flattened rice)","Salt - to taste","1/2 cup Horse Gram Dal (Kollu/ Kulith)","Sunflower Oil - as required for greasing","1/2 cup White Urad Dal (Split)","1 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","1 1/2 cups Foxtail Millet"], product_ids: [2304,929,4609,2307,2308,503,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Horsegram And Foxtail Millet Idli recipe, wash and Soak Urad dal with methi seeds with enough water ","Soak them for a minimum of 6 hours or leave it overnight","Wash the soak the poha in a bowl of water for 20 minutes before grinding the idli batter.Transfer the urad dal and methi","Transfer this into a mixing bowl in which the batter will be mixed and set aside","Next transfer the horse gram into a mixer-jar and grind into a smooth paste using a little water","Add this to the bowl having the ground urad dal","Likewise grind the millets along with the poha and transfer it to the bowl in which the batter is going to be mixed","Bring all the ground mixtures together in a bowl and mix thoroughly to get a uniform batter ✅"] },
