"veg_lebanese_mihshi_malfuf_recipe_stuffed_cabbage": { title: "Veg Lebanese Mihshi Malfuf Recipe (Stuffed Cabbage Leaves)", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup White garbanzo - soaked","1 Cabbage (Patta Gobi/ Muttaikose)","1 teaspoon Black pepper powder","3 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","Parsley leaves - few","1 cup Homemade tomato puree","Salt - to taste","4 Lemons - freshly squeezed","1 Onion - chopped","3 tablespoon Parsley leaves - chopped","1 Garlic","1 cup Basmati rice - washed"], product_ids: [545,2307,924,48,465,2300,476,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Veg Lebanese Mihshi Malfuf recipe, clean cabbage and parboil head in a large kettle of water just lo","Place the cabbage leaves in a colander as you peel them.Pit out the large stem from the bottom of the cabbage","This will help the leaves to roll easily","Mix all the ingredients mentioned under stuffing in a bowl","Lay each cabbage leaf separately on a cutting board, cut out the stem if it's too thick","Pour tomato puree and water over the cabbage rolls","Add salt, pepper powder and oil","Serve Veg Lebanese Mihshi Malfuf along with Mujaddara for your weekend dinner with friends and family ✅"] },
