"eggless_tutti_frutti_cake_recipe": { title: "Eggless Tutti Frutti Cake Recipe", serves: "3", time: "65 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoon Milk Powder","1 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)","80 grams Butter - at room temperature","1 teaspoon Baking powder","1 teaspoon Corn flour","pinch Salt - pinch of salt","1/2 teaspoon Baking soda","2 tablespoons Raisins","Milk - milk as required","pinch Food Color - pinch of yellow food colour (optional)","1 teaspoon Vanilla Extract","1/3 cup Sugar"], product_ids: [2307,8,2314,460,4141,4142,4144,1842], steps: ["To prepare Eggless Tutti frutti cake, prep up all the ingredients and preheat oven to 180 degrees Celsius","Prepare a loaf tin by applying oil on it and dusting with flour.Sift together the dry ingredients- all-purpose flour, wh","Mix very well","For the right consistency, add milk if needed","Add tutti frutti and raisins and at last add white vinegar and then mix it well.Pour the batter into the prepared loaf t","Sprinkle some crushed cardamom if using.Bake in the preheated oven for 30 to 35 minutes at the same temperature.The top ","Then slice and enjoy with Masala Chai or Filter Coffee ✅"] },
"kiwi_basil_lemonade_recipe": { title: "Kiwi Basil Lemonade Recipe", serves: "3", time: "15 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["5 cups Water","Black Salt (Kala Namak) - to taste","2 tablespoons Lemon juice","Ice cubes - as required","Basil leaves - few","2 Kiwi - peeled","2 tablespoons Sugar syrup"], product_ids: [48,2314,2302,927], steps: ["To begin making the Kiwi Basil Lemonade recipe, peel the kiwis and keep them aside.Now add the kiwis along with some bas","Mix everything properly.Now in the same jug, add in the kiwi and basil puree","Mix it well and make sure the puree is mixed with the flavoured water properly.Add in the ice cubes and serve","You can also keep it in the refrigerator to make it chilled","Serve Kiwi Basil Lemonade along with some snacks like Instant Nimbe Avalakki and Baked Masala Namak Para to your guest w"] },
"vegetable_dal_pakor_recipe_dal_bhajiya": { title: "Vegetable Dal Pakor Recipe - Dal Bhajiya", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 Carrot (Gajjar) - grated","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","Salt - to taste","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","1 Onion - finely chopped","2 inch Ginger - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Enos fruit salt","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - small bunch","1/2 cup Yellow Moong Dal (Split) - soaked overnight","1/2 cup Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal) - soaked overnight","1 tablespoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,4143,468,2300,503], steps: ["To begin making the Vegetable Dal Pakora, into a preheated pan roast the fennel seeds till aromatic","Remove from the pan and allow to cool","Once the fennel seeds have cooled crush them coarsely in a mortar and pestle and keep them aside","Add the soaked dals into a mixer grinder","Add very little water and blend to make a coarse batter","Transfer the Dal pakora batter to a mixing bowl and add in the remaining ingredients like the green chillies, ginger, ca","Check the salt and spice levels and adjust to suit your taste","*Method for pan frying the pakora'sPreheat the kuzhi paniyaram pan, add about a teaspoon of oil in each of the cavities."] },
