"cream_cheese_swirl_brownies_recipes": { title: "Cream Cheese Swirl Brownies Recipes", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["2 cups Dark chocolate","1/2 cup Butter (unsalted)","540 grams Britannia Cheese Spread - Classic - at room temperature","1 teaspoon Vanilla Extract","1/4 teaspoon Salt","2 large Whole Eggs","1/2 teaspoon Vanilla Extract","1/4 cup Caster Sugar","1/2 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)","1 Whole Egg - at room temperature","1/2 cup Caster Sugar"], product_ids: [2314,4142,4144,4145,4148,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Cream Cheese Swirl Brownies Recipe, prep all the ingredients and keep them ready","For the cream cheese layerInto a large mixing bowl add the cream cheese, castor sugar, vanilla extract,egg and beat well","This will take about two minutes","Keep aside.For the Brownie LayerInto a double boiler place a heat proof bowl","Into the bowl add the butter and dark chocolate and melt the chocolate and butter until creamy and smooth","Add dollops of the remaining brownie batter on top of the cream cheese layer","Use a knife and create swirls.Place the pan in a preheated oven at 180 C.Bake for about 30 minutes or until the brownies","If it comes out with just a few moist crumbs then it is done ✅"] },
"aloo_amritsari_recipe_in_hindi": { title: "Aloo Amritsari (Recipe In Hindi)", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["oil - as per use","1 teaspoon coriander powder","1/2 teaspoon Kashmiri red chilli powder","1 teaspoon celery","2 inches ginger - cas","2 onions - cut directly","1/2 small Spoon garam masala powder","salt - as per taste","1/2 teaspoon turmeric powder","2 tomatoes - finely chopped","4 Potatoes - cut into wedges","4 sprig coriander - finely chopped"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,973,1841,2300,473,476], steps: ["To make Aloo Amritsari, first heat the oil in a pressure cooker","After heating, add celery and cook for 10 seconds","Add onion, green chillies, ginger and garlic after 10 seconds","Cook onion until it becomes soft","After the onion softens, add tomatoes and cook until it becomes soft","After softening, add potatoes","After adding, add 1/2 cup of water, salt, mix and close the cooker","Cook until 2 cities come and then turn off the gas ✅"] },
"karela_aur_baingan_ki_sabzi_recipe_bitter_gourd_br": { title: "Karela Aur Baingan Ki Sabzi Recipe - Bitter Gourd Brinjal Sabzi", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 Karela (Bitter Gourd/ Pavakkai) - wash","1 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)","6 Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant) - thinly sliced","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","Salt - to taste","1 Onion - chopped","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1/2 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 tablespoons Sunflower Oil","1/2 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)"], product_ids: [1,929,2307,973,4143,4148,469,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Karela Aur Baingan Ki Sabzi Recipe, wash the bitter gourd, scrape the skin slightly and cut into thi","Remove the seed and white skin at center.Wash, cut the brinjal into thin slices and keep immersed in salted water to pre","Add the bitter gourd slices to oil and fry on medium flame until it turns darker color and shrinks a little","This is done to remove bitterness.Remove the fried bitter gourd from oil and keep it aside","Add the chopped brinjal to the same oil and cook until it turns soft and changes color","Remove from oil and keep it aside.To the same oil in pan, add mustard seeds, cumin seeds and fenugreek seeds","Once it splutters, add chopped onion and saute until translucent.After the onions are translucent, add turmeric powder, ","Mix well and cook for about 2 to 3 minutes.Now add both the cooked veggies along with salt to taste and very little wate"] },
"greek_style_briami_recipe_simple_vegetable_stew_re": { title: "Greek Style Briami Recipe (Simple Vegetable Stew Recipe)", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["Salt - to taste","2 Stalks Celery - chopped","2 Carrots (Gajjar) - diced","2 Onions - sliced","2 sprig Parsley leaves - finely chopped","Black pepper powder - to taste","1 Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant) - cut into wedges","2 tablespoons Extra Virgin Olive Oil - for cooking","1 Green zucchini - cut into wedges","4 cloves Garlic - chopped","1/2 cup White broad beans - soaked over night","1 cup Cauliflower (gobi) - cut into small florets"], product_ids: [545,2307,924,2314,460,465,1841,468], steps: ["This will take a good 5 -7 minutes.In the meantime, pressure cook the white beans in a pressure cooker for 4 whistles an","Release its pressure naturally and keep it aside.Back into the pan where the potatoes and carrots are being cooked, add ","Add the pureed tomatoes and cooked white beans","You can add some water to adjust the consistency of the stewSeason it with salt and pepper and simmer for 20 minutes by ","Serve the Greek Style Briami as a main course for any party or can be relished during a Sunday Lunch meal ✅"] },
"tattha_poyaru_sambar_recipe_black_eyed_beans_samba": { title: "Tattha Poyaru Sambar Recipe - Black Eyed Beans Sambar", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","1/4 cup Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal)","2 Dry Red Chilli","2 teaspoon Sambar Powder","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi) - + 1/4 teaspoon","2 cloves Garlic","1 Tomato - finely chopped","1/8 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/4 cup Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","1 Onion - finely chopped"], product_ids: [545,930,929,2307,2308,973,2300,503], steps: ["To begin making the Thatta Payaru Sambar recipe, wash the toor dal with water twice and drain the excess water from the ","Set the cooked dal aside until the pressure releases.In a large pot, add about 3 cups of water and bring it to boil over","Add black eyed beans and 1/4 teaspoon of turmeric powder to the boiling water.Cook the beans with lid uncovered until th","Drain the excess water from the beans and set aside.Heat a medium sized pan on the stove over medium heat","Add oil to the pan","Once the oil is hot, add the ingredients mentioned under tempering which includes asafoetida, dry red chilli, fenugreek ","Fry them for few seconds, till the mustard seeds splutter and urad dal turns golden.Add chopped onions, tomatoes and sau","Once the onions are soft, add sambar powder, red chili powder, and salt ✅"] },
"wheat_rava_halwa_recipe": { title: "Wheat Rava Halwa Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Brown Sugar (Demerara Sugar)","1 cup Jaggery","1 cup Broken Wheat (Dalia/ Godumai Rava)","1 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","1-1/2 tablespoon Ghee"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,4140,2300], steps: ["To begin with Wheat Rava Halwa, first crush the jaggery and keep it aside","Heat ghee in a pan and then fry the cashew nuts until golden brown.Take water in a heavy bottom pan","Once water starts to boil, add the wheat rava in a pan.Cover and cook till the rava is soft","Make sure that it should not be mushy","(it took 20 minutes for me to cook as my rava was a bit big)Add the sugar and jaggery to it","Let it melt and it will turn into a syrup form","This process will take about 5-8 minutes","Mix everything well till the syrup gets absorbed by the rava.Add ghee and mix everything again and cook for 2 minutes mo"] },
