"almond_pottukathalai_no_recipe_no_almond_chana_dal": { title: "Almond Pottukathalai No Recipe - No Almond Chana Dal", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1/4 cup Ghee","1/4 cup Almond Meal (Badam Powder)","1 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi) - crushed","1/4 cup Jaggery - powdered","1 cup Roasted Gram Dal (Pottukadalai)"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,4140,2300], steps: ["Keep kneading until you can make lemon size balls of the Badam Pottukadalai Ladoo","The heat in your hands will help all the ingredients to bind itself together","So resist adding more ghee","Add only if neededRoll them into lemon size balls and the Badam Pottukadalai Ladoo are ready","Store the ladoos an air tight container in the refrigerator.Serve Badam Pottukadalai Ladoo as a tea time snack along wit","You can also pack them in your snack box ✅"] },
"konkani_style_sol_kadhi_recipe_kokum_flavored_coco": { title: "Konkani Style Sol Kadhi Recipe - Kokum Flavored Coconut Curry", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["4 cloves Garlic - crushed","1 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","8 Kokum (Malabar Tamarind) - soaked with 1 cup water","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/2 cup Fresh coconut","2 Dry Red Chillies","1 sprig Curry leaves","1 pinch Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2311,9,973,920,2300], steps: ["Strain the paste through a fine sieve to extract fresh coconut milk from it","Keep it aside.Heat a pan with a teaspoon of oil, crackle the jeera and mustard seeds","Then add in the curry leaves and dry red chillies","Sprinkle hing and add in the garlic as well","Saute for about 20 seconds.Once done pour this over the milk, add the kokum liquid as well and then garnish with some co","Serve the Konkani Style Sol Kadhi Recipe along with Steamed Rice and Karate Batate Puddi Sagle Recipe (Konkani Style Bit"] },
"kokum_saar_recipe_traditional_maharashtrian_kokum": { title: "Kokum Saar Recipe - Traditional Maharashtrian Kokum Drink", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["3 tablespoon Kokum (Malabar Tamarind) - unsweetened juice","3 tablespoon Jaggery - grated","2 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","5-6 Curry leaves","2-1/4 cup Water","2-3 Dry Red Chillies - broken or 1-2 green chillies","1 tablespoon Ghee","1/2 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","Salt - as required (if using unsalted juice)","2 teaspoon Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped"], product_ids: [930,2307,2311,2314,4140,973,920,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Maharashtrian Kokum Saar Recipe, first add Kokum juice, water and jaggery in a saucepan","add salt if using unsalted juice.Heat on a low flame till the jaggery dissolves (Do not bring the kokum saar to boil)","Keep it on low while we prepare the seasoning for the kokum saar.Heat ghee in a small tadka pan","Add the cumin seeds, hing curry leaves, chillies and mix","Allow the seasoning to crackle.Take off the heat and pour it over the Kokum Saar.Take the Kokum Saar off the heat, garni","Serve the Maharashtrian Kokum Saar along with Matki Chi Rassa Bhaji , Steamed Rice and Kachumber Salad for your everyday"] },
