"kongunadu_cucumber_juice_recipe_spicy_tonji_eggpla": { title: "Kongunadu Cucumber Juice Recipe - Spicy & Tonji Eggplant Juice", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥤 Smoothie", all_ingredients: ["10 Small Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant)","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","4 cloves Garlic","Salt - to taste","1 Tomato - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","2 Dry Red Chillies - (adjust according to the heat of the chilli)","5 Curry leaves - tear them roughly","1 Dry Red Chilli - cut it into smaller pieces","2 teaspoons Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal)","1/2 cup Tamarind Water"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2311,4140,973,1842], steps: ["Cook this until the brinjals have softened","Once the brinjals have softened, add the freshly ground rasam masala, 2 more additional cups of water and salt to taste.","Once it comes to a brisk boil, turn the heat to low and simmer the rasam for about 10 minutes until you notice it starts","To Season The RasamHeat ghee in skillet or tadka pan on medium heat; add the mustard seeds and allow to to crackle","Add the red chili, curry leaves and asafoetida and keep it going for a few seconds.Pour the seasoning into the Kathirika","Serve the Kongunadu Brinjal Rasam along with steamed rice topped with ghee and a poriyal like Beetroot Curry ✅"] },
