"moong_bhajji_recipe_moong_fritters": { title: "Moong Bhajji Recipe-Moong Fritters", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["Sunflower Oil - for deep frying","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","4 cloves Garlic","1 inch Ginger - chopped","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 Onion - chopped","1/2 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1 cup Yellow Moong Dal (Split) - soaked in water for 2 hours","4 Green Chillies - chopped"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,2300,503,476,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Moong Bhajji Recipe, first wash and soak the moong dal for an hour.Drain the water from the dal comp","Do not use any water for grinding.Add this dal mixture in a mixing bowl along  with onion and coriander leaves.Heat the ","Fry till golden brown","Fry the Bhajji in batches ✅"] },
"kumror_chokka_recipe_kaddu_kala_chana_sabzi_pumpki": { title: "Kumror Chokka Recipe - Kaddu Kala Chana Sabzi | Pumpkin Chickpea Curry", serves: "3", time: "150 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["2 Potato (Aloo) - peeled and diced","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","500 grams Kaddu (Parangikai/ Pumpkin) - peeled and diced","1/2 teaspoon Kalonji (Onion Nigella Seeds)","1 teaspoon Salt - or to taste","1 Tomato - finely chopped","2 Green Chillies - slit","2 teaspoons Panch Phoran Masala","2 tablespoons Mustard oil","2 Dry Red Chillies","1 Bay leaf (tej patta)"], product_ids: [545,2307,2314,973,2300,503,473,476], steps: ["To begin making the Kumror Chokka Recipe, prep all the ingredients and keep ready.Cook the soaked kala chana/ chickpeas ","Add water such that it is just about 1-1/2 inches above the chickpeas","Pressure cook for 4 whistles and turn the heat to low","Simmer for another 15 minutes and turn off the heat","Cover the pan for a few minutes to fasten the cooking of the potatoes.Once cooked and roasted, transfer to a bowl and ke","In the same pan; add the remaining mustard oil","Add the mustard seeds, kalonji, asafoetida, ginger, green chillies, bay leaf and red chillies","Stir fry for a few seconds.Add the pumpkin, tomatoes, panch phoran, turmeric powder and salt ✅"] },
"spicy_jalapeno_scrambled_eggs_recipe": { title: "Spicy Jalapeno Scrambled Eggs Recipe", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["2 Onions - chopped finely","2 Pickled Jalapenos - deseeded and cubed finely","8 Cherry tomatoes - deseeded and chopped","1 teaspoon Salt - adjustable per requirement","5 Whole Eggs - beaten","1 teaspoon Whole Black Peppercorns - freshly ground","2 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped finely","2 tablespoons Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [545,930,3,2307,973,1842,4148,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Spicy Jalapeno Scrambled Eggs recipe, firstly heat oil in a wide pan over medium heat.Add onion, tom","Do not overcook as the vegetables will turn mushy.Add beaten eggs and cilantro to the vegetables","Season with salt and pepper.Leave them undisturbed for about 2 minutes, until the eggs form a layer.Fold the eggs occasi","Serve Spicy Jalapeno Scrambled Eggs with toast and a hot cup of tea or coffee for breakfast.Serve Spicy Jalapeno Scrambl"] },
"oats_peas_tofu_stuffed_paratha_recipe": { title: "Oats, Peas & Tofu Stuffed Paratha Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🌅 Breakfast", all_ingredients: ["Water - for kneading","1/2 cup Instant Oats (Oatmeal) - soaked in 2 tablespoon water","1 Red Bell pepper (Capsicum) - finely chopped","1 cup Tofu - crumbled","1 inch Ginger - chopped","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 Onion - chopped","1 Green Chilli - chopped","Sunflower Oil - for kneading","1 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1/2 cup Green peas (Matar)"], product_ids: [1,930,2307,973,1840,2300,503,4152], steps: ["To begin making the Oats, Peas & Tofu Stuffed Paratha Recipe we will first prep all the ingredients and keep them ready.","In a large mixing bowl, add the flour and salt","Add water little at a time and knead to make a soft and smooth dough.Once all the flour has come together, drizzle a tea","Cover the dough and keep aside.We will now proceed to make the stuffing.Heat a skillet on a medium heat with some oil, a","Then add in the chopped onion, green chillies, bell peppers and peas","Saute them till it is half cooked","Add in the crumbled tofu, soaked oats and all the spice powders, cook them well on the medium heat till the raw smell of","Keep it aside.Divide the dough portions into medium lemon size balls ✅"] },
