"karnataka_style_mangrasa_recipe_raw_mango_chutney": { title: "Karnataka Style Mangrasa Recipe - Raw Mango Chutney Recipe", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Red Chilli powder","1/2 cup Water - (adjust)","2 teaspoons Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 Mango (Raw) - (half ripen Totapuri cultivar)","Salt - to taste","1/2 cup Jaggery - grated","2 teaspoons Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","1/2 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1/2 cup Coconut Oil"], product_ids: [1,929,2307,9,2314,973,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Karnataka Style Mango Rasa Recipe | Mangrasa, remove the skin of mangoes and cut the mango into smal","Keep this aside for further use.In a tadka pan,  add fenugreek seeds and dry roast until you get nice aroma","Keep this aside to cool.To the same pan, add cumin sauté well on medium heat for a minute or till fragrant","Switch off the heat and keep aside.Once the fenugreek and cumin seeds cool down, transfer them into a mixer jar and grin","Now add the ground masala powder and sauté for a minute","Now add hing and fry for about 30 seconds.Next, add mango slices and cook on medium flame for 5 minutes","Now add grated jaggery, red chilli powder and salt to the cooked mango rasa.Add water to this mango rasa and cook for 5 ","Switch off the flame.Cool the mango rasa or mangrasa and store in airtight container ✅"] },
