"andhra_style_aratikaya_vepudu_recipe_raw_banana_dr": { title: "Andhra Style Aratikaya Vepudu Recipe - Raw Banana Dry Sabzi", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoon Sesame powder - roasted","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","Curry leaves - few","3 cloves Garlic","3 Raw Banana","Sunflower Oil - as required","1/2 teaspoon Rasam Powder"], product_ids: [2307,2308,973,503,920,27,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Andhra Style Aratikaya Vepudu Recipe, wash and peel the raw bananas and chop it into thin slices","Keep the chopped slices in a bowl filled with water until its ready to use","This will prevent from it turning back.Drain the water","To the raw banana slices add salt, turmeric powder, red chilli powder and rasam powder","Toss it and mix it well such that the masala gets coated well to the slices.Heat oil in a heavy bottomed pan, add mustar","When the mustard seeds splutter, add garlic and curry leaves","Saute till the garlic is done","Later, add the coated raw banana pieces to the pan and toss them gently ✅"] },
