"amarnath_suji_oats_dhokla_recipe": { title: "Amarnath Suji & Oats Dhokla Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 Ginger - grated","1 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","1 teaspoon Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","Red Chilli powder - for garnish","200 grams Green Amaranth Leaves - finely chopped","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 teaspoon Sunflower Oil","1/2 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","2 cups Sooji (Semolina/ Rava)","40 grams Rolled Oats Or Instant Oats","2 teaspoons Enos fruit salt"], product_ids: [2307,2314,460,973,4142,4143,920,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Amaranth Sooji & Oats Dhokla Recipe, we will first roast the semolina (sooji)","In a wok, dry roast the semolina until you get a slightly roasted flavor","Roast on medium heat for about 3 to 4 minutes taking care not to brown the semolina (sooji)","Once roasted, transfer to a large mixing bowl and keep aside.Next we will cook the amarath leaves","Add the chopped amaranth leaves into the same heavy bottomed pan or wok, sprinkle some salt and stir-fry the leaves unti","Make sure to evaporate any excess water that gets released while cooking the greens","Once cooked, allow the amaranth leaves to cool down and keep aside.Once the leaves are cooled, we will make the sooji oa","In a large mixing bowl where you have kept the roasted semolina, add the oats, the salt, the asafoetida, the cooked amar"] },
"postal_millet_lemon_rice_recipe_lemon_honey": { title: "Postal Millet Lemon Rice Recipe-Lemon Honey", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","Salt - to taste","1 cup Foxtail Millet","1 inch Ginger - grated","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - a small bunch finely chopped","1/4 cup Raw Peanuts (Moongphali)","1 Lemon - juiced","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 sprig Curry leaves - roughly chopped","1/4 cup Carrot (Gajjar) - chopped"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,4143,48,468,503], steps: ["To begin making the Lemon Millet Recipe, make sure you have some cooked millets ready","It helps using a day old millet as the grains will be separated out well","To cook millets, add the cup of millets in a pressure cooker, add 1-1/2 cups of water and pressure cook for couple of wh","Once cooked the millets should be grainy.Keep the remaining ingredients handy, as this recipe will be made in a jiffy.He","Allow them to crackle and the dal and the peanuts to get roasted well until it gets a golden brown color","Turn the heat to low, cover the pan and allow the lemon millet to steam along with the seasonings for a couple of minute","Check the salt and spice levels and adjust to suit your taste.Turn off the heat and stir in the chopped coriander leaves"] },
