"murgh_palak_recipe_chicken_in_a_palak_gravy": { title: "Murgh Palak Recipe - Chicken In A Palak Gravy", serves: "3", time: "75 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["2 Green Chillies","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","Salt - a pinch","1 Onion - chopped","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 tablespoon Ghee","2 cups Water","1 Tomato - chopped","1 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","Salt - to taste","3 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1/4 cup Fresh cream"], product_ids: [929,545,930,2307,2308,2314,4140,973], steps: ["To begin making Murgh Palak Recipe, we have to first marinate the chicken, In a bowl, add curd, chicken pieces, mix well","Add the cleaned palak leaves to a pressure cooker with a teaspoon of water and salt","Pressure cook for 1 whistle and release the pressure immediately by running the pressure cooker under tap water","Remove the lid of the pressure cooker so that the cooking process stops","Do not drain the water","To make the palak puree, add the cooked palak along with ginger, garlic, green chillies and make a smooth Palak Puree fo","Keep it aside","In a kadai, add 1 tablespoon of oil ✅"] },
