"spicy_quinoa_upma_recipe": { title: "Spicy Quinoa Upma Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1/8 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","Salt - as per your taste","1 cup Quinoa - organic","1 Tomato - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Ginger - finely grated or chopped","1 Onion - finely chopped","1/2 cup Green peas (Matar) - steamed","1 sprig Curry leaves","4 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 Green Chillies - slit lengthwise"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,973,2300,503,920,476], steps: ["To begin with Spicy Quinoa and Oats Upma Recipe, dry roast the quinoa in a large pan for about 3 to 5 minutes on medium ","Once they get a roasted aroma, set them aside.In the same heavy bottomed pan, add a tablespoon of olive oil on medium-lo","When the cumin seeds begin to sizzle, add onions and saute it until the onions turn translucent and become soft.Add the ","Sprinkle salt according to your taste and pour in 2 cups of water to the tomato onion mixture and bring the water to a b","Once the water is boiling, add the roasted quinoa and allow them cook for about 4-6 minutes on medium heat","Stir gently on low heat to get rid of any lumps","Cover the Quinoa upma with a lid and allow it cook for another 10 minutes until all the water is absorbed and the quinoa","You can optionally sprinkle some lemon juice and serve warm.Serve the Quinoa Upma along with Coconut Chutney, a glass of"] },
