"peshawari_karahi_gosht_recipe": { title: "Peshawari Karahi Gosht Recipe", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["3 Tomatoes - chopped","1 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","Ghee - for cooking","3 Dry Red Chillies","1 inch Ginger - chopped","2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","Salt - to taste","2 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","500 grams Mutton - with bones","1 Green Chilli - chopped","4 cloves Garlic - chopped","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2314,4140,973,4142,2300], steps: ["Serve the Peshawari Karahi Gosht Recipe can be made any day along with some hot phulka or tandoori roti and jeera rice ✅"] },
"tofu_stir_fry_curry_recipe": { title: "Tofu Stir Fry Curry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥡 Indo-Chinese", all_ingredients: ["300 grams Tofu - cut into squares","2 tablespoon Light soy sauce","1 inch Ginger - julienned","Salt - to taste","1/2 cup Water","1 Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - cut into one inch squares","1/2 cup Mixed vegetables - like broccoli","1 tablespoon Rice Wine Vinegar","1-1/2 tablespoon Corn flour","1 Onion - cut into one inch squares","6 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1 tablespoon Tomato Ketchup"], product_ids: [545,2307,2311,2314,973,1840,1842,1843], steps: ["To begin making the Tofu Stir Fry Curry, first make the red chilli paste, for this soak 3 dried red chilies for 30 mins ","Keep the red chilli paste aside.Heat oil in a non-stick pan and add ginger, garlic and green chilies","Saute on high heat for 30 seconds and add the onions.Cook the onions for 2-3 minutes","The onions should start to become translucent but still be crunchy","Check the salt and spices and adjust to suit your taste","The Tofu Curry is now ready to be served.Serve the Tofu Stir Fry Curry along with a bowl of brown rice and a Beet Carrot"] },
"tandoori_aloo_tikka_recipe_indian_spiced_roasted_s": { title: "Tandoori Aloo Tikka Recipe - Indian Spiced Roasted Smoked Potatoes", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["300 grams Baby Potatoes - boiled & peeled","1/4 cup Hung Curd (Greek Yogurt)","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/4 cup Mint Leaves (Pudina) - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","Salt - to taste","1 Coal - for giving a smoked flavour","1 tablespoon Kasuri Methi (Dried Fenugreek Leaves)","4 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","2 tablespoons Gram flour (besan)","1 tablespoon Ghee - for cooking","1 inch Ginger - finely chopped"], product_ids: [929,2307,2308,2314,4140,4142,946,473], steps: ["Keep this aside in the same pan","Next step is the give the Tandoori Aloo Tikka a smoked flavour","Place a large piece of coal on the gas flame and allow it to turn red hot.Place a katori in the center of the tandoori a","It will begin to emit smoke ✅"] },
"bajra_dal_cheela_recipe_spicy_pearl_millet_lentil": { title: "Bajra & Dal Cheela Recipe (Spicy Pearl Millet & Lentil Crepe Recipe)", serves: "3", time: "445 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Green Moong Dal (Whole)","Salt - salt to taste","1/2 cup Bajra (seeds)","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - few","1 inch Ginger - grated","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","1/2 cup Black Urad Dal (Whole)","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1/2 cup Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,503,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Bajra & Dal Cheela Recipe, soak whole green gram, channa dal, bajra and whole urad dal together in e","Grind all the dals and bajra together along with ginger, coriander leaves and chilies in a mixer grinder to smooth batte","The consistency of the batter should not be very think or very thick, but of smooth pouring consistency","Add salt, asafoetida and transfer the bajra & dal cheela batter to a mixing bowl.To make the Bajra & Dal Cheela, preheat","Pour a ladleful of batter on the skillet and spread it in circular motion inside out to make a thin cheela/ crepe","Drizzle a teaspoon of ghee or oil around the sides and inside and cook till it turns golden brown on both the sides","Once done, remove from the pan and serve","Proceed the same way with the remaining cheela batter.Serve the Bajra & Dal Cheela along with Peanut Chutney, a glass of"] },
