"moongphali_bhindi_recipe_okra_and_peanut_stir_fry": { title: "Moongphali Bhindi Recipe - Okra and Peanut Stir Fry", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥡 Indo-Chinese", all_ingredients: ["4 Dry Red Chillies","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 teaspoons Coriander Powder (Dhania)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","4 tablespoons Sunflower Oil","1 Onion - finely chopped","500 grams Bhindi (Lady Finger/Okra)","1 cup Roasted Peanuts (Moongphali) - coarsely ground","1 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)"], product_ids: [1,930,2307,461,973,2300,503,476], steps: ["To make Moongphali Bhindi Recipe, first wash and pat dry okra","Cut okra into half lengthwise removing the stems","Heat oil in a heavy-bottomed pan over medium heat","Once the oil is heated, add the dry red chilies and chopped onions","Saute the onion over medium heat till they turn golden brown in color.Now add the chopped okra along with ground peanuts","Stir to combine all the ingredients well","Cover the pan with a lid and cook the vegetable over the low heat till it is cooked and tender","Once the Bhindi is half way through the cooking process, open the lid and give it a gentle stir ✅"] },
