"herb_mushroom_bruschetta_recipe": { title: "Herb Mushroom Bruschetta Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["3-4 Cherry tomatoes - quartered","10 to 12 Button mushrooms - cleaned and sliced","Mint Leaves (Pudina) - half a bunch","Salt and Pepper - to taste","4-5 cloves Garlic","1 Baguette","1 Lemon"], product_ids: [545,3,2307,4143,48,946,1850,2302], steps: ["To begin the Herb Mushroom Bruschetta Recipe, let's start with making the topping for the bruschetta.Blitz together mint","Alternatively, you can mince the mint and garlic with a sharp knife and a chopping board.To prepare the mushrooms, heat ","Saute the cleaned and sliced mushroom until all the moisture has evaporated and the mushroom is dry.At this point, we wi","Continue to cook for a minute and turn off the heat.To toast the baguette, slice the baguette and brush both the sides w","Bake the slices in a preheated 180 C oven for 10 minutes or until the baguette is golden brown and lightly crisp ✅"] },
"maharashtrian_style_surnachi_koshimbir_recipe_yam": { title: "Maharashtrian Style Surnachi Koshimbir Recipe-Yam Salad", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥗 Salad", all_ingredients: ["300 grams Elephant yam (Suran/Senai/Ratalu) - cut into thin and small pieces","2 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","4 tablespoons Fresh coconut - grated","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 Onion - chopped","1 pinch Sugar","1 Lemon juice","2 Green Chillies - chopped","2 tablespoons Sunflower Oil","2 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 pinch Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [930,2307,9,2314,973,48,2300,473], steps: ["To begin making the Surnachi Koshimbir Recipe, wash, peel and cut the yam into 1 inch cubes","In a pressure cooker, combine the yam along with 1/2 a cup of water and pressure cook for 4 whistles","Turn off the flame","Allow the pressure to release naturally","Once the pressure has released, drain the water and keep the yam aside","Heat a shallow pan with oil on medium flame, add the boiled yam and stir fry, until the outsides get crispy","Add a pinch of salt and continue to fry till it gets a brown colour","Drain on an absorbent paper ✅"] },
