"one_pot_vangi_bath_recipe_using_preethi_electric_p": { title: "One Pot Vangi Bath Recipe Using Preethi Electric Pressure Cooker (Brin", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant) - finely chopped","1 Curry leaves","1 teaspoon Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","2 tablespoons Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","Salt - to taste","1 cup Rice - washed","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","3 Dry Red Chilli","1/4 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)"], product_ids: [929,930,2307,2308,973,4148,469,503], steps: ["We begin making the One Pot Vangi Bath Recipe, we will start by roasting of vangi bath spice powder","Place a pan on medium heat and roast condiments well until you get a good aroma","Once the spices are roasted, allow it to cool down and then blend it in a spice grinder","Blend the spices in the Zodiac spice mixer grinder","The next step is to make the vangi bathFirst, we will stir fry the brinjal and cook it until soft and then add the spice","The electric pressure cooker is a great piece of equipment - as you can set the time and simply continue to do your work","Heat a bit of oil in the pressure cooker pan","Add the mustard seeds and allow it to crackle ✅"] },
