"zucchini_salad_with_barbecue_sauce_dressing_recipe": { title: "Zucchini Salad with Barbecue Sauce Dressing Recipe", serves: "3", time: "10 min", category: "🥗 Salad", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Lemon juice","1 Carrot (Gajjar) -  cut into thin strips","2 teaspoons Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1/2 Yellow Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - cut into thin strips","2 teaspoons Sesame seeds (Til seeds) - white","Salt - to taste","1/2 Red Bell pepper (Capsicum) - cut into thin strips","1 teaspoon Red Chilli flakes","1 teaspoon Mixed Herbs (Dried)","1 Green zucchini -  cut into thin strips","3 tablespoons Barbeque sauce"], product_ids: [2307,2314,973,48,1840,468,1844,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Zucchini Salad with Barbecue Sauce Dressing Recipe, cut all the vegetables into thin strips","Combine them all and allow it to chill in the refrigerator.To make the Barbecue Sauce Dressing, in a bowl combine, the b","Mix the dressing well.In a mixing bowl, toss the vegetables with the Barbecue Sauce Dressing and serve it in a bowl","Garnish with mixed herbs and sesame seedsServe this Zucchini Salad with Barbecue Sauce Dressing Recipe along with Beetro"] },
"barnyard_millet_sweet_pongal_recipe_kuthiraivali_s": { title: "Barnyard Millet Sweet Pongal Recipe (Kuthiraivali Sakkarai Pongal)", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Jaggery","3 tablespoons Ghee","3/4 cup Barnyard Millet","1 pinch Edible camphor (pacha karpooram)","2 tablespoons Cashew nuts - halved","1/4 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","1/4 cup Yellow Moong Dal (Split)"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,4140,503,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Barnyard Millet Sweet Pongal Recipe (Kuthiraivali Sakkarai Pongal), dry roast the barnyard millet an","Once you can smell the roasted aroma coming out, add 3 cups of water and cover the pressure cooker.Pressure cook until y","After three whistles turn the heat to low and simmer for 3 to 4 minutes and turn off the heat","Allow the pressure to release naturally","Once the pressure has released, open the cooker and stir to make a mushy mixture of pongal and keep aside.Meanwhile take","once the jaggery has completely dissolved, strain it and keep aside.Add the jaggery water, the cardamom powder, the edib","Place it on medium heat and keep stirring until well combined.Heat ghee in a small pan; add the cashew nuts and roast th","Add the roasted cashewnuts to the Barnyard Millet Sweet Pongal and stir ✅"] },
"lebanese_style_baked_chicken_and_potatoes_recipe": { title: "Lebanese Style Baked Chicken and Potatoes Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["Fresh Thyme leaves - few sprigs","1 tablespoon Black pepper powder","Rosemary - few sprigs","2 Chicken thighs","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Mint powder (Pudina) - or small bunch fresh mint leaves","4 tablespoon Lemon juice","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 pinch Nutmeg powder","4 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","4 Potatoes (Aloo) - cut into quarters","1 tablespoon Cumin powder (Jeera)"], product_ids: [930,2307,460,4143,48,946,473,921], steps: ["To begin making Lebanese Style Baked Chicken and Potatoes Recipe, rinse chicken thighs well","Pat dry with kitchen towel.Cut the chicken thighs into two","Keep the leg piece whole","Make slits on both sides.Blend together garlic cloves, olive oil, pepper powder, salt, and lime juice.Rub the blend juic","Rub all the spices - cumin, coriander, mint, nutmeg, rosemary,  well all over the chicken pieces.Place the chicken on th","Bake chicken pieces in oven for about 15 minutes","Baste the chicken at regular intervals with its own juices in between to keep it moist.Arrange potato quarters in betwee","Pour all the oil-lemon juice mix ✅"] },
