"mullangi_poriyal_recipe_south_indian_style_radish": { title: "Mullangi Poriyal recipe - South Indian Style Radish Stir Fry", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🥡 Indo-Chinese", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 tablespoon Tamarind Paste","1 teaspoon Sesame (Gingelly) Oil","2 teaspoon Sambar Powder","Salt - to taste","2 tablespoons Fresh coconut - grated","4 Mooli/ Mullangi (Radish) - along with the greens","2 Dry Red Chillies","1 sprig Curry leaves"], product_ids: [2307,2311,9,973,463,920,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Mullangi Poriyal Recipe, Wash the radish properly, chop the greens and keep aside","Cut the mooli/ mullangi  into thin rounds and keep aside.Heat oil in a wok/kadhai","Add mustard seeds and let it crackle.Once it crackles, add curry leaves and dry chillies and allow them crisp up.Once do","Add sliced radish and sauté on high heat for a minute.After a minute add salt, sambar powder, tamarind pulp and mix well","Reduce the heat and cover the pan with a lid","Cook till the radish is soft.Once done open the lid","If there is any water remaining in the Mullangi Poriyal then saute the sabzi on high heat it till the sabzi becomes dry","Garnish with grated coconut and transfer the Mullangi Poriyal into a serving bowl and serve ✅"] },
