"keema_bhindi_masala_recipe_okra_minced_meat_curry": { title: "Keema Bhindi Masala Recipe - Okra & Minced Meat Curry", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["250 grams Bhindi (Lady Finger/Okra) - cut into 1/2 inch pieces","8 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 cup Homemade tomato puree","Salt - to taste","2 teaspoons Coriander Powder (Dhania)","2 teaspoons Garam masala powder","1 tablespoon Kasuri Methi (Dried Fenugreek Leaves)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 Green Chillies - slit","2 Onions - finely chopped","2 tablespoons Mustard oil"], product_ids: [545,930,929,2307,461,973,4143,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Keema Bhindi Masala Recipe - Okra & Minced Meat Curry, first we will roast the bhindi.To make roaste","Once the oil is hot add the bhindi and sprinkle salt to taste.Stir to combine","Keep the ladle in the pan and cover with the lid","Placing the ladle inside the pan helps to keep the lid ajar","This also helps the bhindi to cook well at the same time not get sticky","Saute at regular intervals to cook the bhindi on all sides","Once the bhindi is well roasted and cooked through turn off the heat and keep aside","To make the Keema MasalaInto a pan add oil and once the oil is hot add the onions, green chillies, ginger, garlic ✅"] },
"mushroom_empanadas_recipe": { title: "Mushroom Empanadas Recipe", serves: "3", time: "90 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - chopped","1 Carrot (Gajjar) - grated","8 Button mushrooms - chopped","2 tablespoons Basil leaves - chopped","1/2 teaspoon Salt - or to taste","3 tablespoons Parsley leaves - chopped","1/2 cup Butter (unsalted)","Salt - to taste","1-1/4 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)","1 Onion - finely chopped","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 teaspoon White pepper powder"], product_ids: [2307,2311,924,4141,1840,4144,468,2300], steps: ["To begin making Mushroom Empanadas Recipe, prepare the dough first","Sift the flour and mix flour with salt","Incorporate butter to the flour, using a pastry blender, a fork or a pastry processor, until the mixture is crumbly.Slow","Wrap it with plastic, knead slowly to form a disc and refrigerate for at least 1 hour.In a frying pan heat oil over medi","Add onion and saute until soft.Add carrot, garlic, bell pepper, mushrooms and soy sauce and cook until any water evapora","Line a baking tray with parchment paper.On a floured surface, roll out dough to thin disc","Using a 3-1/2-inch circle cutter cut out circles of dough","Re-roll dough as needed ✅"] },
"uttarkhand_style_mixed_bhaddu_dal_recipe": { title: "Uttarkhand Style Mixed Bhaddu Dal Recipe", serves: "3", time: "340 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","1/4 cup White Urad Dal (Split)","1/4 teaspoon Whole Black Peppercorns","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1/4 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","Salt - to taste","1/4 teaspoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","2 teaspoon Fresh cream","2 Cloves (Laung)","1 Bay leaf (tej patta)","1/2 cup Homemade tomato puree"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2314,4141,1842,503], steps: ["Take a medium wok, heat 2 teaspoons of oil, add bay leaf, cloves, whole black pepper, turmeric powder and red chilli pow","Let it cook for about a minute","Pour tomato puree and let it cook for another 3 minutes","After 3 minutes, add in the ginger garlic paste","Let it cook till the raw smell vanishes.Next, add the boiled dal to wok and simmer for 8 minutes then add the cream.Mean","Pour it over the dal, mix and serve hot.Serve Uttarkhand Style Mixed Bhaddu Dal along with Bharwa Bhindi and Tawa Parath"] },
