"kadai_chole_recipe_dry_chickpeas_masala_with_capsi": { title: "Kadai Chole Recipe- Dry Chickpeas Masala with Capsicum", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Kashmiri Red Chilli Powder","1/2 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 cup Kabuli Chana (White Chickpeas) - Soaked Overnight","1 Tomato - Pureed","2 Onions - diced in chunks","1/2 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)","Salt - to taste","4 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","1 Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1 Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - diced in chunks"], product_ids: [1,930,545,2307,2308,2314,4140,973], steps: ["To begin making Kadai Chole Recipe, first wash and soak the chickpeas for 6 hours or overnight in water.Cook the chana i","It should retain its green colour.Stir in the tomatoes,and all the dry masalas - Coriander Powder, Red chili powder, cum","Once done, transfer the Kadai Chole to a s serving bowl and serve hot.Serve Kadai Chole with Mixed Vegetable Handi, Pudi","You can also add a Gobi Biryani, Dal Makhani and a Moong Dal Halwa and make a perfect north indian menu for parties ✅"] },
