"traditional_maharashtrian_bhakarwadi_recipe": { title: "Traditional Maharashtrian Bhakarwadi Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 pinch Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)","1/2 cup Dessicated Coconut","1 tablespoon Sugar","1/2 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1/2 cup Gram flour (besan)","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","1 tablespoon Poppy seeds","1/4 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1/2 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)"], product_ids: [1,930,545,2307,2308,2311,9,2314], steps: ["To begin making Traditional Maharashtrian Bhakarwadi Recipe, take all the ingredients required to make the dough in a mi","Once the crumbly dough is formed, knead it by applying pressure into a tight dough.Cover the dough with a damp kitchen t","Brush the roti with tomato ketchup/tamarind paste and spread the filling of masala powder all over the roti.Roll tightly","Take them out once done and absorb excess oil by putting them on a kitchen towel.Once all the bhakarwadi are done and co","These bhakarwadi stay good for a couple of weeks.Serve Traditional Maharashtrian Bhakarwadi Recipe over tea time with Ma"] },
