"nandan_kozhi_recipe_kerala_style_chicken_curry": { title: "Nandan Kozhi Recipe - Kerala Style Chicken Curry", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1 inch Ginger - minced","3 Onions - sliced","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","500 grams Chicken - curry cut","2 tablespoons Coconut Oil","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 teaspoon Chicken masala - (you can use other too but I prefer eastern masalas for kerala style preparations)","2 Cloves (Laung)","4 Tomatoes - chopped","Curry leaves - Handful","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,9,2314,973,2300,920], steps: ["To begin making the Nandan Kozhi recipe, firstly heat oil in a large heavy bottom pan heat oil on medium flame","Add onions, ginger, and garlic and sauté till the onion is deep brown and well cooked","While the onions are being sauted, in a separate pan, on slow flame dry roast the grated coconut to a golden brown colou","Keep aside to cool slightly","This is will also help in dry spices infusing some of their flavour in the roasted coconut","Once cool, grind to a smooth paste using little water.Once the onions have turned deep brown, add the dry spices - chick"] },
"penne_with_roasted_eggplant_and_mint_pesto_recipe": { title: "Penne With Roasted Eggplant And Mint Pesto Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍝 Pasta", all_ingredients: ["1/4 cup Pine nuts","1 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","3/4 cup Mint Leaves (Pudina)","1 cup Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant) - chopped","2 cups Penne pasta","Salt - to taste","Salt and Pepper - to taste","1/2 cup Basil leaves","1/2 cup Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1/2 cup Mint Pesto","2 tablespoons Parmesan cheese"], product_ids: [2303,2307,4145,946,4148,469,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Penne With Roasted Eggplant And Mint Pesto, first prepare the pesto, by blending together mint, basi","Pulse it a couple of times, till coarse.Then, slowly drizzle in the olive oil and blend once more.Stir in salt, pepper a","The pesto can be stored in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to a week.To cook the penne, bring a deep, h","Add a splash of olive oil and a teaspoon of salt to it and drop the penne into it.Cook for 7-8 minutes on a medium heat ","Drain through a colander, drizzle some olive oil, toss and set aside until ready to use.Place a pan on the heat, add som","Place the sliced aubergine/eggplant in the pan and cook covered for 8-10 minutes till the eggplant is cooked through","You can take the lid off in between and flip the sliced eggplant.When the eggplant is fully cooked, take the lid off, ad","Toss well, until the pesto coats all the penne.Serve the Penne With Roasted Eggplant And Mint Pesto hot, topped with sha"] },
"mango_panna_cotta_with_fruit_cream_recipe": { title: "Mango Panna Cotta With Fruit Cream Recipe", serves: "3", time: "140 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["2 teaspoons Agar agar - strands","1/2 cup Double Cream","70 ml Heavy whipping cream","Mixed fruits - your choice","1/2 cup Milk - whole milk","1 cup Mango Pulp (Puree)","3 tablespoons Sugar"], product_ids: [1,2314,2300,4141], steps: ["Keep on stirring at intervals while the cream mixture comes to a gentle boil and sugar gets completely dissolved.Meanwhi","At any point of time mixture should not come to a rolling boil; rather should be at a constant boil","The mixture should be smooth.Now, pour this prepared warm Panna Cotta either into individual glasses/bowls or in any con","You can use a hand blender or stand mixer with whip attachment.Switch off before the peaks appear on the cream","Whip for about 1-2 minutes.Now add the flavored cream gently and whip it again at the lowest speed for 2-3 minutes.Gradu","This will help in reducing the chilling time ✅"] },
