"spicy_mullangi_thogayal_recipe_radish_chutney": { title: "Spicy Mullangi Thogayal Recipe (Radish Chutney)", serves: "3", time: "54 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/4 cup Fresh coconut","Salt - to taste","2 teaspoons Sesame (Gingelly) Oil","1 cup Mooli/ Mullangi (Radish) - grated","20 grams Tamarind - soaked in water","2 teaspoons Black Urad Dal (Split)","1 teaspoon Black Urad Dal (Split)","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/4 cup Curry leaves","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2311,9,463,503,920,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Mullangi Thogayal recipe, heat a pan over medium heat","Add the Urad dal and red chillies and roast until dal is lightly browned","Once roasted, add the grated radish, salt, coconut, turmeric powder and asafoetida","Saute until the radish (mullangi) is softened","Once softened, add the cooked mullangi thogayal ingredients into the turbo chop along with the soaked tamarind and make ","Once done, transfer to a serving bowl.For the tadka, heat oil over medium heat; add the mustard seeds and urad dal and a","Stir in the curry leaves and pour the tadka over the Mullangi Thogayal","Serve Mullangi Thogayal along with Tomato Onion Sambar, Elai Vadam and Steamed Rice for a wholesome weekday meal ✅"] },
"mavinakayi_chitranna_recipe_spiced_raw_mango_tempe": { title: "Mavinakayi Chitranna Recipe - Spiced Raw Mango Tempered Rice", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - a small bunch","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","2 sprig Curry leaves","Salt - to taste","1/2 teaspoon Black Urad Dal (Split)","2 Green Chillies - slit","1 teaspoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","1/2 teaspoon SSP Asafoetida (Hing)","1 Mango (Raw) - grated","1 tablespoon Gingelly oil","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 cups Cooked rice - (leftover works fine)"], product_ids: [1,930,2307,2308,973,4143,503,920], steps: ["To begin making the Mavinakayi Chitranna Recipe, we will first prepare the rice.If you don't have day-old rice, cook you","This helps in ensuring the rice doesn't get soggy, sticky and clumpy","Follow Steamed Rice Recipe - Pressure Cooker & Saucepan Methods to cook rice.Next, heat gingelly oil in a heavy bottomed","Add the mustard seeds, chana dal, split urad dal and roast the dals on medium flame until the dals turn golden brown in ","This will take about 2 minutes","Once the mangoes have softened, add the cooked rice, salt to taste and stir well to combine","The Mavinakayi Chitranna makes a great picnic lunch too ✅"] },
