"dal_shorba_recipe_indian_style_lentil_soup": { title: "Dal Shorba Recipe - Indian Style Lentil Soup", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🍵 Soup", all_ingredients: ["Salt - as required","2 teaspoons Coconut Oil","1/2 teaspoon Dry ginger powder","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Lemon juice","1/2 teaspoon Black pepper powder","1 Onion","1/3 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1/4 cup Yellow Moong Dal (Split)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 cups Water","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - for garnishing"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,9,973,48,2300,503], steps: ["To begin making Dal Shorba (Lentil Soup), we have to first wash the moong dal.Next, pressure cook the moong dal for 2 wh","Release the pressure naturally","Once cooked, mash the dal well or puree it with hand blender","Keep aside.Heat a pan with teaspoon of oil, add finely chopped onion and garlic","Saute until translucent.Pour the mashed dal along with 2 cups of water","Mixe well and keep it aside.To prepare the tempering, add a teaspoon of oil in a tadka pan","Once the oil is hot, add cumin seeds and allow it to crackle","Turn off the flame.Pour this tempering over the Dal Shorba and garnish with chopped coriander leaves ✅"] },
"sabudana_khatti_meethi_namkeen_recipe": { title: "Sabudana Khatti Meethi Namkeen Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Raw Peanuts (Moongphali)","1 teaspoon Rock Salt","15-20 Cashew nuts","1 tablespoon Sugar - powdered","8-10 Curry leaves","15-20 Raisins","1/2 cup Sabudana (Tapioca Pearls)","1/2 teaspoon Whole Black Peppercorns - ground","Sunflower Oil - to fry"], product_ids: [2307,8,2314,13,1842,503,920,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Sabudana Khatti Meethi Namkeen Recipe, in a Kadai heat some oil","Drop one pearl of sabudana in hot oil to test if it is heated optimally","If it rises instantly to the surface, the oil is ready to fry.Add sabudana to oil and let the sabudana fry and puff up f","Remove sabudana on a plate lined with a paper towel to absorb extra oil.In the similar way, fry the peanuts till golden ","Be careful not to over fry them for they will taste bitter.Remove the fried peanuts on the plate lined with paper towel ","Add them to the peanut-sabudana plate.Then add raisins to the same pan and toss it in oil till they puff up","Enjoy whenever hunger kicks in","Serve Sabudana Khatti Meethi Namkeen during evening along with Irani chai recipe ✅"] },
