"paneer_gassi_recipe": { title: "Paneer Gassi Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","1 Onion - finely sliced","3 Cloves (Laung)","2 Curry leaves","15 Whole Black Peppercorns","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","500 grams Paneer (Homemade Cottage Cheese) - cut into cubes","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds"], product_ids: [929,930,2307,2308,2311,9,2314,4140], steps: ["To begin making the Paneer Gassi Recipe, soak the ball of tamarind in hot water for 10 minutes.In a heavy bottomed pan a","Roast coriander seeds, cumin seeds, fenugreek seeds, dried red chillies, pepper corns one by one until fragrant","Be careful to roast on a low flame so as not to burn the spices","Once roasted remove from pan and set aside to cool.In the same pan, add sliced onions, garlic and roast until onions sta","Now add freshly grated coconut and continue to roast until coconut starts to turn golden brown","Remove from pan and set it aside.Squeeze out the water from the tamarind and throw away the seeds","Once all the roasted spices and the onion-coconut mix has cooled, add them all to a blender and blend into a smooth past","Add cinnamon, cardamoms, cloves and saute until fragrant ✅"] },
