"aloo_bonda_recipe_deep_fried_snack_with_potato_fil": { title: "Aloo Bonda Recipe (Deep Fried Snack With Potato Filling)", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","Water - as required","2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","Sunflower Oil - for deep frying","5 Potatoes (Aloo) - boiled","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil - hot","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Lemon juice","2 tablespoons Rice flour","1 teaspoon Ajwain (Carom seeds)","10 Curry leaves - chopped","1 cup Gram flour (besan)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,48,920,473,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Aloo Bonda recipe, firstly we will make the potato filling.Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a heavy bottomed","Add the mustard seeds and once they splutter add the cumin seeds.Add the green chillies, ginger, hing, curry leaves, tur","Take it off the heat","Add the lime juice and coriander leaves and mix","Keep aside to cool.Heat a deep fry pan for deep frying the bondas.In a mixing bowl add the ingredients under ‘for the ba","Make small balls out of the potato mixture.Dip each ball in the batter and deep fry on low to medium heat till golden br","Serve Aloo Bonda with Dhaniya Pudina Chutney, Date Tamarind Chutney or any other chutney of your choice ✅"] },
"rajasthani_gunday_pickle_recipe_bird_lime_pickle": { title: "Rajasthani Gunday Pickle Recipe (Bird Lime Pickle)", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1/2 tablespoon Red Chilli powder","Salt - to taste","3 tablespoons Mustard oil","500 grams Gunde (bird lime)","1 teaspoon Split Methi Seeds (Methi Kuria)","1 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf) - roasted and crushed","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon Split Mustard Seeds (Rai Kuria)"], product_ids: [929,2307,973,48,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To Prepare Rajasthani Gunde Ka Achaar, boil the gunde ni water until soft, drain the water, remove the seeds and keep it","Once heated, stir in the asafoetida, the achaar masala and red chilli powder","Once cooled completely, store the Gunde Ka Achaar in pickle bottle/ceramic/glass container","Store the Gunde Ka Achaar in the refrigerator for 3 to 4 weeks or even upto a month","Since this a more like a fresh pickle, it only stays for a month or two.Serve Rajasthani Gunde Ka Achaar as an accompani"] },
"spicy_goan_style_mushrooms_recipe": { title: "Spicy Goan Style Mushrooms Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["Sunflower Oil - for deep frying","250 grams Button mushrooms","3 cloves Garlic - grated","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1/4 cup Rice flour","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 cup Sooji (Semolina/ Rava)"], product_ids: [2307,460,973,1850,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Spicy Goan Style Mushrooms Recipe, first wash the mushrooms and pat them dry","Cut them into halves lengthwise along with the stem.If the mushroom is big, cut them into quarters.In another bowl, comb","Add the Mushrooms into this coating mixture and toss them well","Heat a couple of tablespoons of oil in a shallow frying pan over medium heat","Add the sooji coated mushrooms into the pan and fry it on low flame, flipping over occasionally until crisp and browned ","This would take about 15 minutes","Once browned and crispy, remove from the pan and serve.Serve the Stir Fried Spicy Goan Style Mushrooms Recipe as an appe","You can also optionally top these mushrooms with sliced onions, green chilies and lemon to add to the tang.Serve Spicy G"] },
