"flourless_mud_pie_recipe": { title: "Flourless Mud Pie Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Chikki (peanut brittle) - optional","65 grams Butter (unsalted)","65 grams Caster Sugar","115 grams Dark chocolate","50 grams Almond Meal (Badam Powder)","1/2 teaspoon Vanilla Extract","3 Whole Eggs - (or Flax meal Egg Replacer)"], product_ids: [2314,4144,4148,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Flourless Chocolate Mud Pie Recipe, we will first melt the chocolate using the double boiler method","First, place a saucepan on medium heat with 250 ml of water and bring it to a gentle simmer","Place a heat proof bowl over the saucepan such that the water is not in direct contact with the heatproof bowl","We will henceforth refer to this arrangement as bain-marie.In the bain-marie, melt bite size pieces of chocolate and but","We will now take the bowl off heat and set it aside until partially cooled.Meanwhile, let's separate the egg whites and ","Note: Add the Flax meal Egg Replacer at the above stage.Further, fold the beaten egg whites gently into the chocolate mi","This step is crucial to help maintain the consistency of the mud pie","(Skip this step for egg free cake)Now, we shall pour the chocolate mixture into a lined and greased spring foam tin and "] },
"gujarati_kachariyu_recipe_spiced_sesame_and_coconu": { title: "Gujarati Kachariyu Recipe - Spiced Sesame And Coconut Ladoos", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Jaggery","1 teaspoon Dry ginger powder","12 Dates - black one","1 cup Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","1/4 cup Melon seeds","1/2 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","5-6 Dried Figs - chopped","2 tablespoons Ghee","1/4 cup Badam (Almond) - chopped","3/4 cup Dessicated Coconut","Nutmeg powder - A generous pinch"], product_ids: [2307,9,2314,4140,2300], steps: ["To begin making Gujarati Kachariyu Recipe, first we will prepare the filling.Place a skillet or kadai on the heat","Add ghee, once melted add chopped dates and figs to it","Cook this, stirring sometimes, till they turn mushy and stewed, and start leaving sides of pan to come together as a bal","Pulse it again a couple of times till it mixes well.You will notice that the sesame seeds and coconut has released its o","If held in a fist the mixture should come together lightly","If this does not happen pulse it a few more times.Put a spoonful of Kachariyu mixture in the well of your palm, lightly ","Repeat till you have formed all the ladoos.You can roll them in desiccated coconut or finely chopped almonds for garnish","Store the Kachariyu in an airtight box and serve them as a festive ladoo on any occasion or enjoy them as a mid-morning "] },
