"traditional_shahi_tukda_recipe_hyderabadi_double_k": { title: "Traditional Shahi Tukda Recipe - Hyderabadi Double Ka Meetha", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoons Pistachios - chopped","3/4 cup Sugar","2 tablespoons Badam (Almond) - chopped","Saffron strands - a few","1/2 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","2 liter Milk","1 teaspoon Rose water","1/4 cup Sugar","1 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","1/4 cup Water","10 Whole Wheat Brown Bread","1 tablespoon Rose water"], product_ids: [2307,2314,4140,4141,4143,2300], steps: ["To begin making Traditional Shahi Tukda Recipe - Hyderabadi Double Ka Meetha we will first make the rabri.Into a saucepa","It's important to keep scraping down the cream and adding it back to the condensing milk.The mixture will begin to thick","Hence it is extremely crucial to ensure you stay close to the pan and keep stirring.Once the milk has reduced to half of","Now add the cardamom powder and the rose water to the rabri and stir well to combine","For the sugar syrupInto a saucepan add water and sugar","Stir util the sugar dissolves","Allow the sugar syrup to boil for a few minutes","Add the cardamom powder and rose water, stir and turn off the heat ✅"] },
