"ulva_charu_recipe_speci_andhra_horse_gram_rasam": { title: "Ulva Charu Recipe - Speci Andhra Horse Gram Rasam", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍵 Soup", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Horse Gram Dal (Kollu/ Kulith) - uncooked","Curry leaves - handful","1 Dry Red Chilli","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/3 cup Fresh coconut - grated","2 sprig Curry leaves","3 Dry Red Chillies","Salt - to taste","1/2 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","1 Onion - chopped","1 Green Chillies","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,9,973,2300,503,920], steps: ["To begin with the Ulava Charu Recipe, wash and soak the horse gram overnight.The next morning, transfer the soaked and d","Ensure the horse gram is boiled well.Turn off the heat and allow the pressure to release naturally","Open the pressure cooker and set the boiled horse gram aside","To make the masala for the Ulava Charu In a mixer jar, combine the coconut, onion, tomatoes, curry leaves red chillies, ","In a heavy bottom pan, heat oil and add the freshly ground masala for the Ulava Charu","Cook this masala for about 6-8 minutes stirring constantly.When the oil begins to come to the surface, add the horse gra","Let the Ulava Charu boil for about 5-6 minutes","Check the salt and seasoningsTransfer Ulava Charu into a serving bowl ✅"] },
"dudhi_dal_gosht_recipe_mutton_with_bottle_gourd_le": { title: "Dudhi Dal Gosht Recipe-Mutton With Bottle Gourd & Lentils", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["6 Whole Black Peppercorns","1 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 Tomato - finely chopped","5 Amchur (Dry Mango Powder) - whole","5 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped to garnish","1 tablespoon Ghee","1 tablespoon Ginger Garlic Paste","50 grams Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal)","50 grams Masoor Dal (Whole)","Sunflower Oil - as required","Salt - to taste","2 teaspoons Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [1,545,930,2307,2308,2314,4140,973], steps: ["To begin making the Dudhi Dal Gosht recipe, mix all the dals in a pressure cooker and cook till it is properly cooked an","Once it is done, blend with a hand blender.Next, boil mutton with a little salt and water in a pressure cooker for 15 mi","Add all the whole spices including bay leaf, whole pepper corns, cinnamon stick and cumin seeds","Cook them for about 30 seconds and add finely sliced onions and cook till they become slightly brown in colour","(Make sure you do not burn them)Next, add ginger garlic paste, red chilli powder, cumin powder, turmeric powder, coriand","Add the chopped bottle gourd, tomatoes, mix everything properly and let it cook till the bottle gourd is half cooked","Once it is done, add whole mint leaves to it","Now add the boiled mutton, mixed daal and cook for 5 minutes.Now add whole amchur and lemon juice to it ✅"] },
"paneer_darts_momo_recipe": { title: "Paneer Darts Momo Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)","Salt - to taste","Water - to knead","1/2 teaspoon Chaat Masala Powder","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","100 grams Paneer (Homemade Cottage Cheese) - cut into 1/2 cm cubes","1/2 teaspoon Tandoori masala -  Everest Brand","1 tablespoon Fresh cream","1/2 teaspoon Lemon juice","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [2307,4141,973,48,4145,4152,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Paneer Tikka Momo Recipe, first let’s make the dough.For the Momo doughIn a mixing bowl, add maida, ","The dough should be non sticky, smooth and firm","Set aside for 15 minutes","Heat a pan on medium-high flame, place the paneer tikka pieces and cook for about 3-4 minutes","Turn off the flame, transfer the paneer tikka into a bowl and set aside ✅"] },
