"cauliflower_tortilla_recipe": { title: "Cauliflower Tortilla Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1 Cauliflower (gobi)","1 teaspoon Black pepper powder","1 Whole Egg","Salt - to taste"], product_ids: [2307,465,4148,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Cauliflower Tortilla Recipe, wash the cauliflower head and cut them into large florets.Grate the flo","Once the grated cauliflower florets are steamed, allow them to cool.While it is cooking, preheat the oven to 180 degree ","You need to remove as much moisture as possible from the cauliflower.Transfer the dry cauliflower into a clean dry bowl","Add egg, salt and pepper powder, whisk well to combine.Transfer one portion of the mixture, onto a baking sheet lined wi","Spread the mixture with your fingers into tortilla shape","You can make the cauliflower tortillas thick or thin as per your preference.Bake the cauliflower tortillas in the prehea","Next add ginger garlic paste and cook till the saw smell of the paste is gone.Add green chilies and tomatoes and cook ti","Finally add soya granules (pre soaked in water) ✅"] },
"vegetarian_thai_massaman_curry_recipe": { title: "Vegetarian Thai Massaman Curry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["2 teaspoons Palm sugar - or brown sugar","1 teaspoon Tamarind Paste","1 Stalk Lemon Grass - chopped","2 cloves Garlic","1 Spring Onion Greens - finely chopped","300 ml Coconut milk","1 Carrot (Gajjar) - cut lengthwise into 1 inch thin pieces","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","Salt - to taste","1 inch Galangal - or ginger","4 tablespoons Roasted Peanuts (Moongphali)","1/2 teaspoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,2311,9,2314,973,4141], steps: ["To begin making the Vegetarian Thai Massaman Curry Recipe, we will first dry roast the ingredients","Place all the ingredients for roasting in small roasting pan","Roast them on medium heat, until you can smell all the aromas coming through - about 3 to 4 minutes","Once roasted, turn off the heat and keep it aside.The next step is to make the masaman curry paste","Give all the ingredients a stir and bring it to a brisk boil for 3 to 4 minutes","Adjust the consistency of the curry by adding more water if requiredOnce the ingredients come to a brisk boil, turn off ","Check the salt and spice levels and adjust to suit your taste","Transfer to a serving bowl and serve the Vegetarian Thai Massaman Curry along with Jasmine Stick Rice for weeknight dinn"] },
