"andhra_style_peanut_chutney_recipe_with_tomatoes": { title: "Andhra Style Peanut Chutney Recipe With Tomatoes", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","1 cup Roasted Peanuts (Moongphali) - with skin removed","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 sprig Curry leaves","2 Tomatoes - finely chopped","3 cloves Garlic","1 teaspoon Sunflower Oil","5 Dry Red Chillies"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,973,503,920,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Andhra Style Peanut Chutney Recipe, on a low heat, dry roast the peanuts and red chillies together t","Peel the blanched tomatoes and keep aside to cool.Once peanuts and tomatoes are cool, Add them to a mixer grinder along ","Add a little water if required","Check the salt and adjust to suit your taste","Transfer the Peanut Chutney to a bowl.The final step is to make the Tadka.In a small pan, heat oil and add mustard seeds","Once they splutter, add the urad dal and curry leaves","Saute for about 1-2 minutes till the dal is browned and crunchy.Add the Tadka to the Peanut Chutney and serve.Serve the "] },
"drumstick_dal_recipe": { title: "Drumstick Dal Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["2 Drumstick - cut into 3 inch pieces","1 Onion - sliced","1 teaspoon Kashmiri Red Chilli Powder","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","3 Dry Red Chillies","Salt - to taste","2 Green Chillies - slit","1 cup Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal)","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","2 teaspoon Ghee","2 Tomatoes - roughly chopped"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,4140,973,464,2300,503], steps: ["To begin making the Drumstick Dal, in a pressure cooker combine the toor dal along with onions, tomatoes, chili powder, ","Allow the pressure to release naturally","Once the pressure has released, open the cooker and give the dal a quick stir","Adjust the consistency to your liking","Pressure cook Drumsticks along with 2 tablespoons of water and a pinch of salt for two whistles and release the pressure","Cooking drumsticks separately retains their nutrition and color.Add the cooked drumsticks to the dal and give it a stir","Check the salt and seasonings and adjust according to taste.The next step is to make the tadka","In a tadka pan, add ghee and allow it to heat; add the mustard seeds and allow it to crackle ✅"] },
"kabuli_chana_chaat_high_protein_snack_of_chikki_ch": { title: "Kabuli Chana Chaat - High Protein Snack of Chikki Chaat", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1 Cucumber - finely chopped","3 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","1 Potato (Aloo) - boiled and finely chopped","Salt - to taste","1/2 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)","3 tablespoon Aloo Bhujia","2 Onions - finely chopped","2 cups Kabuli Chana (White Chickpeas) - soaked for 8 hours","2 teaspoons Chaat Masala Powder","1/2 tablespoon Lemon juice","2 Tomatoes - finely chopped","3 Green Chillies - finely chopped"], product_ids: [1,545,482,930,2307,973,48,2300], steps: ["To begin making Kabuli Chana Chaat Recipe, soak the chickpeas for 8 hours","Pressure cook the chickpeas along with a little salt for about 25 to 30 minutes and keep aside","Click here to know How To Cook Legumes in a Pressure Cooker.Boil the potatoes in the pressure cooker and cook until soft","Once done, peel and chop the potatoes","Allow it to cool completely.In a Salad Mixing Bowl, add boiled and cooled chickpeas","Make sure that the chickpeas are drained and no additional water is present","Add chopped onion, tomato, boiled potatoes, and cucumber to it.Season the Chana Chaat with chopped green chilies, freshl","Add salt to taste.Finally toss the Kabuli Chana Chaat well ✅"] },
