"kavuni_arisi_payasam_recipe_black_rice_kheer": { title: "Kavuni Arisi Payasam Recipe - Black Rice Kheer", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Black Rice","3 cups Water","3 cup Milk","3 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","10 Cashew nuts","Raisins - a handful","2 teaspoon Ghee","1/2 cup Sugar"], product_ids: [2307,8,2314,4140,4141,2300], steps: ["To begin making Kavuni Arisi Payasam Recipe, wash and soak the black rice overnight","The next morning transfer the black rice along with the water and  pressure cook for 5 whistles, turn down the flame and","Turn off the flame","Allow the pressure to release naturally","If you want to make Kavuni Arisi Payasam the same day, soak the black rice for an hour and pressure cook for 15 whistles","Once the pressure releases, slightly mash the rice with a ladle.Heat a deep bottom pan on medium heat, add the milk and ","To this add crushed Cardamom and sugar and stir well","Cook and stir until it thickens like a porridge and switch off the flame ✅"] },
"pumpkin_dal_with_garlic_tadka_recipe": { title: "Pumpkin Dal with Garlic Tadka Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["250 grams Kaddu (Parangikai/ Pumpkin) - peeled and chopped","1/4 cup Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal)","4 cloves Garlic","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","1/4 cup Masoor Dal (Whole)","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","Salt - to taste","1 inch Ginger - grated","1 Bay leaves (tej patta)","2 Green Chillies - slit","1 teaspoon Ghee","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,2314,4140,973,503,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Pumpkin Dal with Garlic Tadka Recipe, we will be cooking all the ingredients for the dal in a pressu","Wash the dal, cut the pumpkin and the remaining ingredients ready.Add all the ingredients into the pressure cooker (exce","Cook until you hear two whistles","After a couple of whistles, turn the heat to low and simmer for a couple of minutes and turn off the heat.Allow the pres","Once the pressure has released, open the cooker and give the dal a stir and transfer to a serving bowl","Check the salt and spices and adjust to suit your taste.For the garlic tadka, heat ghee in a small tadka pan on medium h","Add the cumin seeds, garlic and red chilies","Allow them to roast for a few seconds and pour the tadka over the dal.Serve the Pumpkin Dal with Garlic Tadka Recipe alo"] },
"chicken_mie_goreng_recipe_noodles_tossed_in_srirac": { title: "Chicken Mie Goreng Recipe - Noodles Tossed In Sriracha Sauce", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍝 Pasta", all_ingredients: ["Sunflower Oil - as required","1 Onion - finely sliced","1 Red Bell pepper (Capsicum) - finely julienned","1/4 cup Soy sauce","200 grams Wheat Noodles","1 Whole Egg","Salt and Pepper - to taste","100 grams Chicken breasts - chopped","1 cup Broccoli - chopped into small florets","500 grams Button mushrooms - sliced","1 cup Spring Onion Greens - chopped about 2 inch","4 cloves Garlic - chopped"], product_ids: [2307,2311,1840,1843,4148,2301,1850,476], steps: ["To begin making the Chicken Mie Goreng Recipe, cook noodles as per packet instructions and drain the water","Allow it to cool.Heat oil in a wide bottomed pan/ wok, add garlic and onions and sauté until they turn translucent.Add i","Add in the boiled noodles and toss until the mixture gets coated on all the noodles","Serve hot.Serve Chicken Mie Goreng Recipe along with Crispy Chiili Chicken for a weekend dinner","Also serve Rich Dark Chocolate Mousse to end the meal on a sweet note ✅"] },
"muttai_kuzhambu_recipe_south_indian_egg_curry": { title: "Muttai Kuzhambu Recipe - South Indian Egg Curry", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","6 Garlic - grated","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 Onion - chopped","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","2 Tomato - chopped","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - as required (chopped)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","Sunflower Oil - as required"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,973,4148,2300,476,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Muttai Kuzhambu recipe, boil eggs in enough water in a saucepan and once cooled, remove the outer sh","Boiling of eggs will take 12 to 15 minutes.Cut the eggs lengthwise into two halves and keep aside.Heat oil in a heavy bo","Add mustard seeds and cumin seeds","Once it splutters, add chopped onion and saute well until translucent.Once the onions become soft, add garlic and saute ","Now, add chopped tomatoes and saute until it turns soft and mushy.Add coriander powder, garam masala powder, red chilli ","Add required water for the gravy and cook for few minutes until oil separates.Once the gravy becomes little thick, add t","Do not boil for long time and do not stir often","Once it is done, garnish with coriander leaves and serve hot.Serve Muttai Kuzhambu along with Appam, Steamed Rice or Lac"] },
"bhindi_huli_recipe_south_indian_style_tangy_okra": { title: "Bhindi Huli Recipe - South Indian Style Tangy Okra", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["2 cups Bhindi (Lady Finger/Okra) - chopped","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 tablespoon Coconut Oil","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/2 teaspoon Tamarind Paste","1 teaspoon Sambar Powder","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 cup Onion - chopped or cubed"], product_ids: [2307,2311,9,973,461,2300,476,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Bhindi Huli Recipe (South Indian Style Tangy Okra), wash and dry okra; trim the ends and cut into 1 ","Cube onions and keep aside.Heat oil in a large deep saucepan and once hot, add mustard seeds","As soon as the mustard seeds crackle and pop, stir in the chopped onions and mix well.Add in the turmeric powder, red ch","Mix well and sauté on medium high heat, stirring often until the onions are soft and lightly sautéed or until they chang","Stir in tamarind water or paste along with salt to taste and mix again.Add as much or as little tamarind for flavoring d","Cook on medium high, covered, stirring in between until the bhindi is cooked and semi dry.Taste in between and add salt ","Remove from heat and serve as a side dish with your meal.You can serve Bhindi Huli Recipe (South Indian Style Tangy Okra"] },
