"aava_pettina_majjiga_pulusu_recipe_andhra_style_mo": { title: "Aava Pettina Majjiga Pulusu Recipe - Andhra Style Mor Kuzhambu", serves: "3", time: "35 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Bottle gourd (lauki)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 tablespoon Fresh coconut - chopped into pieces","1 teaspoon Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","1 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt) - whisked","Salt - to taste","1/2 teaspoon Sunflower Oil","Asafoetida (hing) - a pinch","1/4 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds) - a few","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 Tomato - quartered","1 teaspoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)"], product_ids: [545,929,2307,2308,9,2314,973,462], steps: ["Into a pressure cooker, add a cup of water, salt and turmeric powder, potato, carrots, bottle gourd, tomatoes, slit gree","Turn off the heat and allow the pressure to release naturally","In another pan, on a low heat add the cup of whisked curd, half a cup of water, the Aava paste, a pinch of Asafoetida an","Turn off the heat","Do not add salt to the curd mixture when it is boiling, the mixture will curdle","Add salt only after adding the vegetables.After all the vegetables are cooked, add them to the curd mixture along with t","Mix well and simmer the Aava Pettina Majjiga Pulusu for 3 to 4 minutes","Add more salt if required ✅"] },
