"chicken_cheese_stuffed_kulcha_recipe": { title: "Chicken Cheese Stuffed Kulcha Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["Water - to knead the dough","1 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","2 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","250 grams Chicken - minced","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","Salt - to taste","1/3 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1/4 cup Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Active dry yeast"], product_ids: [930,2307,2314,973,4142,4144,4145,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Chicken Cheese Stuffed Kulcha Recipe, we will first make the dough","To make the dough for the Chicken Cheese Stuffed KulchaIn a mixing bowl, combine the whole wheat flour, all purpose flou","Next add water, little by little to knead the dough","We are looking for a smooth soft dough","Bring the kulcha dough together to form a smooth dough with a few drops of cooking oil","Cover the bowl with a damp cloth and rest it in a warm place for about 30-40 minutes or until  the dough has doubled in ","To make the filling for the Chicken Cheese Stuffed KulchaIn a pan heat oil on medium heat, once the oil is hot add the g","Next add all the dry masalas, red chilli powder, cumin powder, black pepper powder, turmeric powder, garam masala powder"] },
