"arbi_ke_patte_ke_pakode_colocasia_leaf_rolls_recip": { title: "Arbi Ke Patte Ke Pakode - Colocasia Leaf Rolls Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","Salt - to taste","1/2 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)","1/2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","Lemon wedges - for garnish","2 cups Gram flour (besan)","Chaat Masala Powder - to sprinkle","Water - as needed","Sunflower Oil - to cook","2 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","10 Colocasia Leaves (Arbi) - medium size"], product_ids: [1,930,2307,2308,973,48,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Arbi Ke Patte Ke Pakode, firstly select the softest and youngest leaves for best taste","Cut the central stem and remove its hard membranes using a knife.Wash them thoroughly and pat dry with a kitchen towel","Set aside.In a bowl, add besan or chickpea flour, salt and red chili powder","Spread the batter generously on the top of the entire leaf.Place another leaf on top of it and repeat the procedure with","If you have large leaves, you can stop at placing 4 leaves, one after the other.Fold the ends from both sides so as to m","Keep applying the batter on the inner side of the swirl also","Repeat the same for all the leaves.Heat water in a steamer and steam the prepared colocasia leaves for about 15 minutes ","The batter is non-sticky after steaming.After cooling to room temperature, cut them into slices using a sharp knife ✅"] },
