"quinoa_vangi_bath_recipe": { title: "Quinoa Vangi Bath Recipe", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","Salt - to taste","2 tablespoons Vangi Bath Powder","2 to 3 Dry Red Chilli","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","10 Curry leaves","1/4 cup Kabuli Chana (White Chickpeas) - cooked","1 cup Quinoa","12 to 15 Cashew nuts - broken","1 tablespoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1 Lemon juice"], product_ids: [2307,2308,973,48,4148,469,503,920], steps: ["To begin making the Quinoa Vangi Bath, firstly wash the quinoa with water and bring 1 cup of quinoa and 2 cups of water ","Serve hot.If you don't have access to Vangi bath powder ✅"] },
"cheesy_mushroom_masala_dosa_recipe": { title: "Cheesy Mushroom Masala Dosa Recipe", serves: "3", time: "330 min", category: "🌅 Breakfast", all_ingredients: ["4 Tomatoes - finely chopped","1 cup Barley (seeds)","1 cup Paneer (Homemade Cottage Cheese) - grated","200 grams Britannia Cheese Block - grated","2 cups White Urad Dal (Whole)","1/2 teaspoon Chaat Masala Powder","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","6 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1/4 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 cups Ragi Seeds","Water - for soaking","Mint Leaves (Pudina) - small bunch"], product_ids: [545,929,2307,2308,973,4143,4145,946], steps: ["The level of water should be an inch above the rice in the bowl","Let it soak for about 6 hours or overnight","Soak the urad dal and fenugreek in water such that all of the dal is completely immersed in water","The level of water should be 2 inches above the dal in the bowl","Let it soak for about 6 hours.After the soaking period, first grind the urad dal into a fine smooth batter","While grinding add just enough water to make it into a very smooth batter","The batter will look fluffy.Grind the rice, ragi, barley into a smooth batter, adding just the required amount of water ","Adding too much water will make the mixture too watery ✅"] },
"orange_date_muffin_recipe": { title: "Orange & Date Muffin Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 Whole Egg - or flaxseed egg replacer","1 cup All Purpose Flour (Maida)","1/4 teaspoon Salt","1 teaspoon Cinnamon Powder (Dalchini)","2/3 cup Dates - chopped","1/2 cup Brown Sugar (Demerara Sugar)","1/3 cup Fresh orange juice","2 teaspoon Baking powder","2/3 cup Walnuts - chopped","1 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1/2 teaspoon Baking soda","1/4 cup Butter (unsalted) - melted and cooled"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,4141,16,4144,4148,2300], steps: ["Stir together all the muffin batter ingredients just until combined","Don't overmix the batter","Fold in the orange rind, dates and walnuts","Spoon the muffin batter into the greased 12 muffins cavities","Place the muffin tray in the preheated oven and bake for 15 to 18 minutes, until done.You will know it's done, when you ","Once the muffins are baked, remove them from the oven and allow them to cool completely","Serve the Orange & Date Muffin at tea time or pack them in your child's snack box ✅"] },
"dhaba_style_dal_palak_recipe": { title: "Dhaba Style Dal Palak Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal) - washed","Salt - to taste","1 Tomato - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","4 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","2 Green Chillies - slit","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","1 Onion - finely chopped","2 cups Spinach Leaves (Palak) - finely chopped","2 inch Ginger - finely chopped","2 Dry Red Chillies","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,4140,973,48,2300,503], steps: ["To begin making the Dhaba Style Dal Palak, add the chopped spinach along with 2 tablespoon of water and pressure cook fo","Release the pressure immediately to keep the fresh green colour of spinach","Keep the spinach aside.Heat oil in the pressure cooker; add the cumin seeds and allow it to crackle","Pressure cook for about 4 to 5 whistles and turn off the heat.Allow the pressure to release naturally","Once done, open the cooker and add the cooked spinach/ palak to the dal","Give it a brisk boil and turn off the heat","Check the salt and adjust to taste accordingly","Transfer the Dhaba Style Dal Palak to a serving bowl.For the tadka, heat ghee in a tadka pan, add cumin seeds, red chill"] },
"bihari_chana_daal_puri_recipe": { title: "Bihari Chana Daal Puri Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped finely (optional)","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 cup Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","Sunflower Oil - to deep fry"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,973,503,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin making Bihari Chana Dal Puri Recipe, pressure cook chana dal with enough water for about 2 whistles or until co","Also do not overcook the dal since it will make the puri mushy","Once chana dal is cool, drain all the water and mash it","It is up to you to mash it completely or leave it grainy.Heat oil in a wide bottomed pan","Add cumin seeds and let it splutter","Then add mashed chana dal and the spice powders and salt","Cook for about 2 to 3 minutes","You can add a little coriander leaves too at this stage ✅"] },
"kolhapuri_akha_masoor_dal_recipe_masoor_dal_in_kho": { title: "Kolhapuri akha masoor dal recipe (masoor dal in kholpuri masala)", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 inch Ginger - chopped","3 teaspoons Dessicated Coconut","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","3 teaspoons Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","1 Onion - chopped","2 cups Masoor Dal (Whole) - soaked for 5 hours","2 teaspoon Kolhapuri Khanda Lasun Masala - or goda masala","4 cloves Garlic - chopped","1 Tomato - chopped"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,9,973,4148,2300,503], steps: ["To begin making the Kolhapuri Akkha Masoor Dal Recipe, lets roast the sesame seeds and dessicated coconut on a hot pan.R","Grind it in the mixer to a smooth powder.Next pressure cook the masoor dal with water and salt for atleast 5 whistle","Allow the pressure to release naturally.Heat a flat skillet with oil, add ginger and garlic and saute until softens","Add chopped onions and saute till they turn translucent.Later add chopped tomatoes and cook until the tomatoes turn mush","Sprinkle salt and the other spice powders and cook until the raw smell goes away.Add ground sesame and coconut powder an","Add cooked masoor dal and add 1 cup of water","Check for salt and leave it to boil in simmer.Serve the Kolhapuri Akkha Masoor Dal Recipe along with Doli Ki Roti or baj"] },
