"creamy_pumpkin_pasta_sauce_recipe": { title: "Creamy Pumpkin Pasta Sauce Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍝 Pasta", all_ingredients: ["1 Red Bell pepper (Capsicum) - finely chopped","500 grams Kaddu (Parangikai/ Pumpkin) - peeled and diced","1 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","Salt - to taste","4 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1/4 cup Britannia Cream Cheese - flavored like jalepeno or peppers works great","200 ml Milk"], product_ids: [2307,4141,1840,4145,2301,2302,2303], steps: ["To begin making the Creamy Pumpkin Pasta Sauce Recipe; first get all the ingredients ready and keep it by the side.Heat ","Sprinkle some salt and stir fry to combine for a couple of minutes","Cover the pan, turn the heat to low and allow the pumpkin and peppers to cook until soft and tender","Do make sure to keep stirring intermittently so the vegetables dont get burnt","You will know the pumpkin is cooked, when you press it down with a fork or a spoon, it will mash itself up.Turn off the ","Now we are ready to blend all the ingredients together into the blender.Note: If your blender does not allow hot ingredi","Once blended, check the salt and pepper levels and adjust to suit your taste ✅"] },
"baked_whole_wheat_masala_baati_recipe_healthy_raja": { title: "Baked Whole Wheat Masala Baati Recipe (Healthy Rajasthani Spiced Wheat", serves: "3", time: "80 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoon Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","2 Green Chillies","1/2 cup Ghee","1 cup Green peas (Matar)","1 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","3/4 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1-1/2 teaspoon Sunflower Oil","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 cup Whole Wheat Flour"], product_ids: [930,2307,2314,460,973,4142,4140,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Whole Wheat Masala Baati, first mix all ingredients mentioned under the ‘For baatis’ in a large mixi","If the dough turns out a touch hard to stiff, add a little milk and knead it till soft to touch.Divide the dough into eq","Cover the dough with a damp cloth and let it rest for half an hour.Meanwhile proceed to prepare the masala filling","For this, place a pan on the heat","Add some oil to it and allow it to get warm","Then add cumin seeds, onions and green chilies to the oil and sauté until onions turn light pink.Next, add ginger garlic","Stir continuously as it cooks, until the raw smell of the spices goes away.Then add peas and cook for 3 minutes until al","Take one portion at a time, and flatten it into a small disc about 2-3 inches in diameter, and keep it in your palm ✅"] },
"carrot_cashew_smoothie_recipe": { title: "Carrot Cashew Smoothie Recipe", serves: "3", time: "25 min", category: "🥤 Smoothie", all_ingredients: ["2 teaspoon Honey","1/2 cup Cashew nuts","Cardamom Powder (Elaichi) - a pinch","2 cups Carrots (Gajjar) - cut into chunks"], product_ids: [2307,2314,4141,468,2300], steps: ["To start making Carrot Cashew Smoothie Recipe, Pressure-cook the carrots and cashew nuts in 2 cups of water for a whistl","Let them cool.Place the cooled carrots, cashew, the cooked carrot broth, and honey in a high-powered blender and blend u","Add cardamom and stir.You can also make this ahead of time and chill in the fridge","Carrot Cashew Smoothie Recipe is a great welcome drink for parties too!Serve Carrot Cashew Smoothie along with Akuri and"] },
