"chutney_chilli_cheese_toast_recipe": { title: "Chutney Chilli Cheese Toast Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🌅 Breakfast", all_ingredients: ["Mozzarella cheese - or cheddar cheese","1/4 cup Red Chilli flakes","1/2 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 cup Mint Leaves (Pudina)","Salt - to taste","1/4 cup Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - chopped","1 Tomato - finely chopped","4 Whole Wheat Brown Bread - whole wheat","1 cup Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","1/2 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","Butter - as required to spread","1/4 cup Fresh coconut - chopped"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,9,973,4143,48,1840], steps: ["To begin making Chutney Chili Cheese Toast, firstly grind all the ingredients mentioned under ‘Chutney’ in a mixer grind","Transfer it to a bowl.Preheat oven at 180 degree C for 10 minutes","Take a baking tray and cover with a foil sheet","Keep it aside.To prepare toast, take a bread slice and cut into 2 or 4 halves.Take a half bread slice and spread butter ","Take a teaspoon of chutney and spread it over the butter nicely.Top the bread slice with some chopped tomato and green c","Arrange bread slices on baking tray and bake it in an oven for about 5-8 minutes.Serve Chutney Chili Cheese Toast along "] },
"railway_mutton_curry_recipe": { title: "Railway Mutton Curry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Ghee","1 teaspoon Mustard oil","1 Mace (Javitri)","1/4 Nutmeg","4 tablespoons Mustard oil","2 Tomato - pureed","1 Onion - thinly sliced","2 Green Chilli - slit lengthwise","1 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","1/2 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)","Salt - to taste","500 grams Mutton"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2314,4140,973,4142], steps: ["Fry the potatoes","Don’t make them brown and fry till the color becomes light golden brown","Remove and keep them aside.Heat oil in the Pressure cooker and once the oil is heated, put the whole Garam masala","Increase the heat to a high and stir continuously to avoid sticking to the bottom","Now reduce the heat to a medium and continue cooking the meat without the lid","The meat will release juices and you can see a thin layer of oil on top of the pieces.Once it gets to this point, add th","Close the lid and pressure cook for 3 to 4 whistle on high heat and then reduce the heat and cook on a low flame for 5 m","After opening the lid add the coconut milk and give everything a good stir ✅"] },
"tandoori_gobi_tikka_recipe": { title: "Tandoori Gobi Tikka Recipe", serves: "3", time: "75 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 Cauliflower (gobi) - cut into large florets","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 cup Hung Curd (Greek Yogurt) - (or greek yogurt)","1/2 teaspoon Ajwain (Carom seeds)","3 tablespoons Gram flour (besan)","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Chaat Masala Powder","1 teaspoon Kasuri Methi (Dried Fenugreek Leaves)"], product_ids: [929,930,2307,2308,2314,973,4142,465], steps: ["To begin making the Tandoori Gobi Tikka Recipe, make sure you have all the ingredients ready","The most important being the hung curd (greek yogurt)","To make the Tandoori Gobi Tikka Recipe, we will first power steam the cauliflower","Power steaming is a process there the vegetable is partially cooked, but when you take a bite, it is edible enough to ea","Steaming the cauliflower helps it to absorb the tikka masala well.To steam the cauliflower, place the florets in a Steam","There are two ways you can make these","If you have a Barbeque Grill then you can grill the Tandoori Gobi Tikka or flavor the Tikkas using the Coal Smoking Meth","This prevents skewers from falling apart while grilling ✅"] },
