"meen_peera_kerala_style_fish_recipe_with_shredded": { title: "Meen Peera (Kerala Style Fish Recipe With Shredded Coconut)", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["3 Green Chillies","1 cup Fresh coconut - grated","2 inch Ginger","2 Kokum (Malabar Tamarind) - for the curry","Salt - to taste","500 grams Sardine fish","10 Shallots","1/4 teaspoon Methi Powder (Fenugreek Powder)","3 clove Garlic","1/4 tablespoon Dry Red Chilli - crushed","1 teaspoon Coconut Oil - adjustable","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)"], product_ids: [929,2307,2311,9,973,2300,920,476], steps: ["To prepare Meen Peera (Kerala Style Fish Recipe with shredded coconut), wash and clean the sardines and marinate it with","Keep aside for 10 minutes.Throw away the kudampuli and wash the fish under running water till cleaned well","Drain all the water","Cut each fish into 3 pieces for better incorporation of flavor.Add the cleaned sardines into a meen chatti (earthenware)","When the mixture is boiling, lower the flame and cook for about 5-6 minutes.Now continue to cook the fish with the lid s","Sauté occasionally and cook till water has reduced.Open the lid completely and continue to cook the fish a medium high f","(Take care not to burn the dish).Serve Meen Peera (Kerala Style Fish Recipe with shredded coconut) with steamed rice and"] },
