"goan_prawns_balchao_recipe_prawns_pickle": { title: "Goan Prawns Balchao Recipe (Prawns Pickle)", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","3 Onions - finely chopped","1/2 cup Tamarind Paste","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","15 Whole Black Peppercorns - pounded","15 Garlic - finely chopped","50 Prawns","1 Lemon","1 teaspoon Salt"], product_ids: [2307,2311,48,1842,2300,476,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Goan Prawns Balchao recipe, soak the tamarind pulp in 1 cup water for atleast 15 minutes.De-vein and","Refer to this video to know how to de-vein prawns.After cleaning, add chilli powder, turmeric powder and mix well","Keep it aside.Meanwhile, let us prepare the masala","Take the tadka pan or any small pan, add asafoetida and 2 teaspoon oil.After 1 minute, add black pepper and mustard seed","After cooling make a paste of this using a mortar and pestle.This masala can even be done and in advance and stored in f","Heat a kadai/pan, add 5 teaspoon oil.Add chopped onion and fry till onions turns mushy","Add garlic and mix","Fry till aroma gets emitted from garlic.Add prawns and mix ✅"] },
"kale_apple_salad_recipe": { title: "Kale Apple Salad Recipe", serves: "3", time: "15 min", category: "🥗 Salad", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Chia Seeds","1 teaspoon Dijon Mustard","Salt - to taste","1 1/2 cups Kale - leaves","1 teaspoon Honey","1/4 cup Badam (Almond) - slivered","1 Apple - chopped into thin slices"], product_ids: [0,2314,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making Kale Apple Salad Recipe, first clean the Kale leaves thoroughly as they contain fine mud particles in it","Drain the water from the leaves and chop the Kale leaves.Mix the Kale leaves with a little salt in a bowl and rest for 5","Mix them well","Now to assemble the salad, take a large salad bowl and add the kale leaves into it","Add the sliced apples, slivered almonds and dijon mustard and honey mix","to the kale and toss the salad well.Sprinkle chia seeds on top and serve cold.Serve Kale and Apple Salad for your sunday"] },
"egg_biryani_recipe_with_coconut_milk": { title: "Egg Biryani Recipe With Coconut Milk", serves: "3", time: "120 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["6 cloves Garlic - minced or grated","1 1/2 cups Water","1/2 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","Salt - to taste","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 Green Chilli - slit down the middle","3 Tomatoes - diced small","2 Onions - thinly sliced","2 cups Coconut milk","1/2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 inch Ginger - minced or grated"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,9,973,4141,4143,946], steps: ["To begin making the Egg Biryani Recipe, we will first set the eggs to boil so they are cooked and kept ready.To boil The","Bring the water to a boil","Allow the eggs to boil in the water for about 3 to 4 minutes","After 3 to 4 minutes, turn the heat to medium and boil the eggs for another 10 minutes","It takes approximately 10 minutes to hard boil the eggs","Turn off the heat","Allow the eggs to cool down completely before you can crack the shell","Peel off the egg shells and keep the eggs aside ✅"] },
