"dates_chocolate_nut_balls_recipe_energy_balls": { title: "Dates Chocolate & Nut Balls Recipe (Energy Balls)", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["30 Pistachios","30 Badam (Almond)","500 grams Dates - seedless","30 Cashew nuts","2 tablespoons Ghee","2 tablespoons Cocoa Powder","1/4 cup Sesame seeds (Til seeds) - roasted (or cocoa powder or coconut)"], product_ids: [9,4140], steps: ["To begin making the Dates Choco Balls Recipe, first grind the seedless dates in a food processor or your mixer","Take care to roast them gently so they turn golden and aromatic, but not burn","Take them out of the ghee and set them aside.In the same pan heat the remaining 1/2 tablespoon of ghee and add the groun","Then, take it off the heat.Now add the roasted cashew nuts, almonds, pistachios, along with the cocoa powder, to the dat","Allow the mixture to cool down.Once it is cool enough to handle, shape of your choice","You can roll the date chocolate mixture into lemon-sized balls for convenience","You can also pop them into lunch boxes, snack on them after exercise and use them to satisfy your sweet cravings too ✅"] },
