"carrot_methi_pachadi_recipe": { title: "Carrot Methi Pachadi Recipe", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/4 tablespoon Mustard seeds","1 Carrot (Gajjar) - grated","1 tablespoon Tamarind Paste","Salt - to taste","1/2 tablespoon Jaggery","1 tablespoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 tablespoons White Urad Dal (Split)","1/4 tablespoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 Dry Red Chillies","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped (adjustable)","100 grams Methi Leaves (Fenugreek Leaves)","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [929,2307,2308,2311,2314,973,468,503], steps: ["To begin making the Carrot Methi Pachadi recipe, heat oil in a tadka pan.Once the cooking oil is hot, add urad dal, cumi","Once the mustard seeds starts to crackle, add in the dry red chillies and saute a bit","Switch off after few seconds.In a kadai, add a bit of oil, once hot, add the green chillies, fresh methi and grated carr","Let it cook for about a minute till the methi wilts a bit.Add tamarind paste and mix it well","Turn off the heat and let the mixture cool down.Once it cools down, transfer the mixture into blender","Add in the jaggery and the required salt","Blend it into a coarse paste but with the help of a bit of water such that the pachadi is not very thick","Pour the tadka over pachadi and serve.Serve Carrot Methi Pachadi along with Beetroot Sambar Recipe and Ghee Rice Recipe "] },
"palak_makhana_recipe_navratri_fasting_vrat_recipe": { title: "Palak Makhana Recipe (Navratri Fasting / Vrat Recipe)", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","2 Tomatoes - diced","300 grams Spinach Leaves (Palak)","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","Salt - to taste","1 cup Phool Makhana (Lotus Seeds)","1 Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","2 tablespoon Milk","1 tablespoon Ghee","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,2314,4140,4141,973,4144], steps: ["We begin the Palak Makhana by washing the spinach thoroughly under running water","Drain the spinach and cook it in a pressure cooker with little bit of turmeric powder, cumin seeds and green chillies fo","Blend it into paste and keep it aside.Roast the makhana with ghee on a flat bottomed non-stick pan","Remove the makhana and in the same pan add little bit of oil and temper the cumin seeds and add the tomatoes.Cook until ","Add the blended spinach mixture along with milk and simmer it for 3 minutes again.Finally, add the makhana and bring it "] },
"mango_curry_recipe_mango_curry": { title: "Mango Curry Recipe - Mango Curry", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 tablespoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","3 Dry Red Chillies","Salt - to taste","Curry leaves - few sprigs","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/4 cup Fresh coconut - grated","2 Dry Red Chillies","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 tablespoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 tablespoon Jaggery","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [1,929,2307,2308,9,2314,973,503], steps: ["To begin making the Mavinakayi Gojju Recipe , into a pressure cooker add the chopped mangoes with a little water and tur","Turn off the heat and allow the pressure to release naturally.To make the masala heat a pan and add the urad dal, chana ","Next add the, red chillies,  fenugreek seeds, cumin seeds and roast till aromatic and turn off the heat","Allow the mixture to cool","Into a mixer grinder add fresh grated coconut, the roasted masala and blend to make a smooth mixture","Next add 3/4th of the cooked mango pieces, jaggery, salt, and pulse it again with the coconut into a coarse paste.The ne","Heat oil in a deep pan and add mustard seeds and let it crackle","Add red chillies and curry leaves and hing.Let the curry leaves crisp up ✅"] },
"sindhi_bhuga_chawal_recipe_sindhi_style_browned_ri": { title: "Sindhi Bhuga Chawal Recipe - Sindhi Style Browned Rice Pulao", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["4 Whole Black Peppercorns - coarsely pounded","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","1 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","2 Green Chillies - slit","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","2 cloves Cloves (Laung)","3 Onions - thinly sliced","2 tablespoons Ghee","1 Bay leaf (tej patta)","1-1/2 cup Rice - washed and soaked"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,4140,973,1842,2300,476], steps: ["To begin making the Sindhi Bhuga Chawal Recipe, wash and soak the rice for a minimum of 30 minutes.In a pressure cooker,","Add 2 cups of waters, the soaked and drained riceClose the pressure cooker and pressure cook the Sindhi Bhuga Chawal for","Once the pressure released, open the cooker and allow the Sindhi Bhuga Chawal to rest for a few minutes before you can s","Check the salt and adjust accordingly","Transfer the Sindhi Bhuga Chawal to a serving bowl and serve hot.Serve this Sindhi Bhuga Chawal Recipe along with Palak "] },
"gluten_free_koloocheh_recipe_persian_date_nut_fill": { title: "Gluten-Free Koloocheh Recipe | Persian Date Nut Filled Cookies", serves: "3", time: "35 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1/3 cup Sugar - (I used organic)","1/2 cup Walnuts - or almonds","1/4 cup Fresh orange juice","2 teaspoons Baking powder","1/2 cup Dates - pitted and chopped","1 teaspoon Vanilla Extract","1/4 teaspoon Salt","1 Whole Egg","1 cup Butter","1/2 teaspoon Cinnamon Powder (Dalchini) - (more if you like)","1-1/4 cups Buckwheat Flour (Kuttu Ka Atta)","1 pinch Salt"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,16,4144,4148,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making Gluten-Free Koloocheh Recipe | Persian Date Nut Filled Cookies, prepare the cookie dough first.Preparati","Add the vanilla and egg and mix until combined","[If the dough is extremely sticky, add more flour (s) to get the right consistency","The dough is a soft dough but should not be sticky]Turn the dough onto a piece of cling wrap and press it into a disk","Wrap and chill in the refrigerator for 30 to 40 minutes, until firm but still flexible.Preparation Of FillingCombine 1/4","Lower the heat and simmer uncovered, stirring often, for 5 to 7 minutes, until the mixture forms a thick paste","Transfer to a plate and let cool to room temperature.Preparation Of KoloochehGrease and line a baking sheet","Pre-heat oven to 180 degree Celsius.To make each cookie, break off a lemon-size piece of the dough ✅"] },
