"andhra_gongura_pulihora_recipe_gongura_puliyodarai": { title: "Andhra Gongura Pulihora Recipe | Gongura Puliyodarai | Spicy Red Rosel", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon White Urad Dal (Split)","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","1/2 cup Roasted Peanuts (Moongphali)","4 Dry Red Chillies","3 tablespoons Sesame (Gingelly) Oil","1 teaspoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","2 teaspoons Salt - to taste","2 sprig Curry leaves - finely chopped","2 tablespoon Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","1/2 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [929,930,2307,2308,2314,973,503,920], steps: ["To begin making the Andhra Gongura Puliyodharai Recipe, prep all the ingredients and keep them ready.Wash the rice well ","Cover the pressure cooker and cook the rice for 2 whistles","After 2 whistles, turn the heat to low and simmer the rice for 3 to 4 minutes and turn off the heat.Allow the pressure t","Once the pressure releases, open the cooker, transfer the rice to a wide place and drizzle a little sesame oil and toss ","We do this, so the rice remains grainy and not sticky.Wash the Gongura leaves, remove the stems and only use the leaves","Once well roasted, turn off the heat and allow it to cool.Once cooled add it to a small jar of the mixer grinder and ble","Keep it aside.In a heavy bottomed pan, heat a few tablespoon of sesame oil over medium heat","Add the mustard seeds, urad dal, chana dal and raw peanuts ✅"] },
