"mixed_millet_and_lentils_adai_recipe": { title: "Mixed Millet And Lentils Adai Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Green Moong Dal (Whole)","1 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1/4 cup Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal)","Water - as required","2 sprig Curry leaves","1/2 cup Jowar Seeds","1/4 cup Masoor Dal (Whole)","Salt - to taste","2 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1/2 cup Kodo millet","1/2 cup White Urad Dal (Whole)","1/2 cup Yellow Moong Dal (Split)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,13,973,2300,503,920], steps: ["To begin with Mixed Millet And Lentils Adai, add all the millets into a bowl","Wash them and soak in enough water for minimum 4 hours","You can soak overnight too.Grind the soaked millets and lentils along with dried red chillies and asafoetida, adding a l","The consistency of the batter has to be slightly thick and not too watery.Heat 1 teaspoon oil in a pan","Saute finely chopped onions, cumin seeds and chopped curry leaves until onions turn soft.Add the sauted onions-cumin-cur","Add finely chopped coriander leaves and salt","Cook on one side with oil dribbled on top and sides.Turn adai on the other side and cook for 10 seconds","Remove adai from tawa, repeat the same procedure for remaining batter.Serve Mixed Millet And Lentils Adai with South Ind"] },
