"sarson_ka_saag_recipe_classic_north_indian_saag_re": { title: "Sarson Ka Saag Recipe - Classic North Indian Saag Recipe", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🥤 Smoothie", all_ingredients: ["Salt - to taste","250 grams Bathua leaves - washed and roughly chopped","1/2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","4 tablespoons Ghee","250 grams Spinach Leaves (Palak) - washed and roughly chopped","1 teaspoon Makki Ka Atta (Yellow Corn Meal Flour)","4 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Garam masala powder","2 inch Ginger - finely chopped","3 Green Chillies - slit into half","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","500 grams Mustard greens - washed and roughly chopped"], product_ids: [930,2307,4140,973,1842,2300,923,476], steps: ["To begin making the Sarson Ka Saag Recipe, we will first steam the leaves together along with a little salt until soft a","For this, you can use a steamer or a pressure cooker.Place all the leaves in the pressure cooker, add a little salt and ","Cover the pressure cooker and cook until you hear one whistle","After the first whistle turn off the heat.Place the cooker under running water and release the pressure immediately and ","This process of releasing the pressure immediately will help keep the greens green.Allow it to cool","You can either puree the saag or use a masher and mish mash the greens to make it soft and mushy","The way you like to present it is purely your choice.Heat a teaspoon of ghee in a heavy bottomed pan; add the ginger, ga","Saute all the ingredients together on low heat until the onions are completely tender and soft and lightly browned.You c"] },
"cheesy_stuffed_mushrooms_with_spinach_recipe": { title: "Cheesy Stuffed Mushrooms With Spinach Recipe", serves: "3", time: "45 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Britannia Cheezza - grated","6 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","6 Button mushrooms - large","2 tablespoons Britannia Cheese Spread - Asli Pepper","3 cups Spinach - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil"], product_ids: [2307,4145,1850,923,2300,2301,2303], steps: ["Do not add salt and cook the spinach, because if you do the spinach will release a lot of water and will take a long tim","Once the spinach is cooked well and we have the right texture, turn off the heat and stir in the Britannia Asli Pepper C"] },
"chicken_with_creamy_mushroom_sauce_recipe": { title: "Chicken with Creamy Mushroom Sauce Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Mixed Herbs (Dried)","1 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","Parsley leaves - a handful","Salt - to taste","2 tablespoons Cheese spread - pepper flavour prefered","1 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 Onion - finely chopped","6 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","3 Chicken breasts","400 grams Button mushrooms - sliced","1/2 cup Fresh cream","1 tablespoon Whole Black Pepper Corns - coarsely pounded"], product_ids: [2307,924,4141,973,4145,1842,2300,1850], steps: ["To begin making the Chicken with Creamy Mushroom Sauce Recipe, firstly wash and clean the chicken well","Heat a grilling pan with oil, add garlic and onions and allow let it cook for until the onions become just about tender","Add the mushrooms and saute the mushrooms for about a minute","Add the chicken breast pieces, sprinkle some salt & cover the pan","Allow the chicken to grill on the pan for about 5 minutes","Keep turning the chicken around while it is cooking","After 5 minutes, add the herbs, black pepper, red chilli powder, cream, cream cheese, salt and parsley.Toss well for 2 m","Transfer the Chicken with Creamy Mushroom Sauce to a serving bowl and serve hot.Serve Chicken with Creamy Mushroom Sauce"] },
"tomato_dosa_recipe": { title: "Tomato Dosa Recipe", serves: "3", time: "285 min", category: "🌅 Breakfast", all_ingredients: ["oil - or ghee ( To make dosa)","1/4 teaspoon fenugreek seeds","water - as per use","1/4 cup white urad dal (split)","1/2 teaspoon cooking soda","salt - as per taste","1 cup rice","3 tomatoes"], product_ids: [545,929,2307,2308,4140,503,2300,2301], steps: ["To make tomato dosa, first wash the rice, fenugreek seeds and urad dal separately","Then soak them all separately for 3 to 4 hours","After 3 to 4 hours, remove water from rice, fenugreek seeds and urad dal and grind it","Add some water to the bitches","Now add chopped tomatoes and grind it a little longer","After grinding it well, take it out in a bowl","Add salt and cooking soda to it and mix","Keep it aside for 10 minutes ✅"] },
"beet_and_avocado_chapati_recipe": { title: "Beet and Avocado Chapati Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["2 cups Whole Wheat Flour - more for dusting","1/4 cup Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","1/4 cup Mint Leaves (Pudina) - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","2 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil - more for cooking","Salt - to taste","1/2 Avocado - mashed","1/2 cup Beetroot - grated","2 tablespoons Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","3 Green Chilli - ground to paste","2 teaspoons Ginger - ground to paste"], product_ids: [930,2307,973,946,470,1849,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making Beet and Avocado Chapati Recipe, into a mixing bowl, add Atta, cumin powder, sesame seeds, chili paste a","Mix well to combine","Bring it all together using your fingers or you can even use a dough hook on your stand mixer on a slow speed.Add some w","After a few seconds you will notice small air pockets popping out","You will notice brown spots around the cooked Beet and Avocado Chapati","Remove from heat and place on a flat plate.Serve Beet and Avocado Chapati Recipe with Punjabi Chana Masala and Masala An"] },
"karigadab_karnataka_style_karanji_gujhiya_recipe": { title: "Karigadab - Karnataka Style Karanji / Gujhiya Recipe", serves: "3", time: "90 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Whole Wheat Flour - or all purpose flour","2 tablespoon Ghee - melted","1/4 cup Sooji (Semolina/ Rava) - fine variety","2 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 handful Rice flour","1/2 cup Roasted Gram Dal (Pottukadalai)","1/4 cup Dessicated Coconut","1/4 cup Sugar","Sunflower Oil - to deep fry"], product_ids: [2307,2308,9,2314,460,4140,2301], steps: ["To prepare Karigadabu – Karnataka Style Karanji recipe, heat ghee in a Tadka pan","Mix wheat flour, rice flour and semolina in a bowl","Pour hot ghee to this flour and semolina mixture evenly","Ghee bubbles up the flour where it comes in contact with it, so pour in the ghee slowly","Mix with fingers after a minute","The mixture will look like bread crumbs","This will ensure you get nice flaky pastry once fried.Now add water to knead the pastry dough","Let the dough be stiff and not too soft ✅"] },
