"homemade_mole_sauce_recipe": { title: "Homemade Mole Sauce Recipe", serves: "3", time: "70 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1 Onion - sliced","1 tablespoon Raw Peanuts (Moongphali)","2 cloves Garlic","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","2 inch Dark chocolate","1 cup Chicken stock","Salt - to taste","1 tablespoon Butter","1 tablespoon Makki Ka Atta (Yellow Corn Meal Flour)","1 tablespoon Raisins","2 Cloves (Laung)","2 Tomatoes"], product_ids: [545,2307,2308,8,2314,1840,4144,1842], steps: ["Add them into a mixer along with star anise, cloves, cinnamon and raisins","Add little water to blitz it into a smooth paste","Keep it aside.Take the tomatoes out and chop them up and blitz them also along with toasted peanuts and chipotle chilies","Heat the pan with butter once the butter starts to melt, add maize flour and keep whisking it to make a roux.Add chicken","Keep whisking till the sauce thickens.Add in the onion paste and tomato paste and bring it to a boil","Add in your seasonings and broken chocolate now and whisk well","Adjust the salt level and boil for 10 more minutes switch off the flame.Use the Homemade Mole Sauce to make Chicken mole"] },
"vazhaithandu_lemon_rasam_recipe_banana_stem_lemon": { title: "Vazhaithandu Lemon Rasam Recipe - Banana Stem Lemon Rasam", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍵 Soup", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Lemon juice","1 tablespoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1/4 cup Arhar dal (Split Toor Dal) - cooked until soft","1 inch Ginger - chopped","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/4 teaspoon SSP Asafoetida (Hing)","Salt - a pinch","1/2 teaspoon Black pepper powder","4 cloves Garlic - sliced","1 cup Water"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2314,4140,973,4142], steps: ["To begin making the Vazhaithandu Lemon Rasam Recipe, whisk the yogurt salt and water in a bowl","Peel the outer skin of plantain stem/Vazhaithandu and discard it","Place the cut banana stem in the yogurt","This prevents it from getting discoloured.Preheat the pressure cooker over medium heat; once heated, add the mustard see","Add a little water and salt and chilli if required according to your taste","Bring the Vazhaithandu Lemon Rasam Recipe to a brisk boil and allow it to froth up - this will take about 4 to 5 minutes"] },
