"high_protein_soya_idli_recipe": { title: "High Protein Soya Idli Recipe", serves: "3", time: "500 min", category: "🌅 Breakfast", all_ingredients: ["1-1/4 cups White Urad Dal (Whole)","1 cup Soybeans (Whole Soya dal)","Water - as required","1 teaspoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","4 teaspoons Salt","1 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","2 cups Idli Rice"], product_ids: [929,2307,2308,503,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making high protein soya idli, we will first make the idli batter","Soak the rice in water, such that the all the rice is completely immersed in water","Let it soak for about 6 hours.Soak the soya bean in water, such that the all the soya bean is completely immersed in wat","Let it soak for about 6 hours.Soak the urad dal, methi seeds and chana dal in water such that all of the dal is complete","Let it soak for about 6 hours.First grind the urad dal into a fine smooth batter","While grinding add just enough water to make it into a very very smooth batter","The batter will look fluffy","Pour this batter into a large container.Next grind the soya bean into a fine smooth batter ✅"] },
"varutharacha_mutta_curry_recipe": { title: "Varutharacha Mutta Curry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","7 Shallots","2 tablespoons Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","1/2 inch Ginger - grated","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1-1/2 tablespoons Sunflower Oil","1 Tomato - finely chopped","Curry leaves - few sprigs","1 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1/2 teaspoon Whole Black Peppercorns","1/4 cup Fresh coconut","1/2 teaspoon Fennel seeds (Saunf)"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,9,2314,973,1842], steps: ["To begin making Varutharacha Mutta Curry Recipe, hard boil eggs in a saucepan","Once they cool down a bit, peel the outer shell and keep the eggs aside","Keep aside till cooled.Once they are cooled, wet grind the spices to a smooth paste by adding a little water","Heat oil in a shallow frying pan","Splutter mustard seeds when the oil is hot","Add ground coconut masala with salt, and enough water","Bring it to a boil","Once the gravy starts boiling, make slits on the surface of hard boiled eggs such that the masala of the curry seeps int"] },
"honey_paneer_recipe_honey_paneer_recipe": { title: "Honey Paneer Recipe - Honey Paneer Recipe", serves: "3", time: "65 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoons cream - or milk","1 tablespoon honey","1 teaspoon cumin seeds","1/2 teaspoon red chilli powder","2 teaspoons oil","1/2 teaspoon cardamom powder","1 cup Paneer - chopped","1/2 teaspoon coriander Powder","salt - as per taste","1 tablespoon Kasuri methi","1/4 teaspoon turmeric powder","1-1 / 2 cup tomato puree"], product_ids: [545,930,929,2307,2314,4141,973,4152], steps: ["To make honey paneer, first heat oil in a pan","In this, add ginger, honey and cook till the honey is boiling","Now add turmeric powder, coriander powder and cook it for 15-20 seconds","After 15 to 20 seconds, add tomato puree, salt, red chili powder, cardamom powder and cook for 2 to 3 minutes","Add milk or cream to it after 2 to 3 minutes","After 1 minute add paneer, kasoori methi and cook it for 3 to 4 minutes","Garnish with green coriander and serve","Serve the paneer with honey along with spinach raita and phulka for dinner ✅"] },
