"thai_red_curry_with_chicken_and_brinjal_recipe": { title: "Thai Red Curry with Chicken and Brinjal Recipe", serves: "3", time: "35 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["Basil leaves - a few","2 tablespoons Thai Red Curry Paste","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","Salt - to taste","300 grams Chicken - boneless pieces","400 ml Coconut milk","2 Brinjal (Baingan / Eggplant) - cut into wedges","2 tablespoons Date syrup","1 cup Broccoli - head","4 cloves Garlic - chopped","1 Stalk Lemon Grass - cut diagnally","1 cup Vegetable stock - or water"], product_ids: [2307,9,4141,48,1843,4148,469,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Vegetarian Thai Red Curry Recipe, get all the ingredients ready.Make the curry paste and keep it asi","Heat oil in a pan and add garlic and stir fry the broccoli and brinjal on high heat for a few minutes until steamed, yet","Sprinkle some salt over the vegetables so that it will cook faster.The next step is to add the Thai red curry base.To th","Stir the red curry paste for a couple of minutes","Add in the chopped chiken pieces and stir fry them for about 5 minutes.Add the coconut milk, vegetable stock, date syrup","Simmer stirring occasionally until the curry thickens a bit about 10 minutes","Check the salt and spice levels and adjust to suit your taste ✅"] },
"no_onion_no_garlic_cabbage_kofta_curry": { title: "No Onion No Garlic Cabbage Kofta Curry", serves: "3", time: "65 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1 green chili - chopped","1/2 tsp turmeric powder","1 sprig of green coriander - cut","1/2 tsp garam masala powder","2 cups cabbage - grated","1/2 cup gram flour","1/2 tsp red chilli powder","1/2 tsp cumin powder","turmeric powder - A pinch","1 to 2 bay leaves","3 to 4 tbsp cream","1/2 tsp cardamom - break it"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,2314,4141,973,4142], steps: ["To make the Cabbage Kofta Curry Recipe, firstly tighten the cabbage and put it in a bowl","Take out the water from it by pressing it","Now add gram flour, green chillies, coriander, cumin powder, turmeric powder, garam masala powder, red chilli powder, sa","Now make small balls of this mixture and keep it aside","Heat oil in a pan","After the oil is hot, add the koftas and fry till it becomes golden","Keep it aside","Now heat oil in a pan ✅"] },
"konkani_style_pathravade_pathrode_recipe_colocasia": { title: "Konkani Style Pathravade/Pathrode Recipe-Colocasia Leaves Snack", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 cups Basmati rice","Coconut Oil - as required","1 tablespoon Green Moong Dal (Whole)","8 Dry Red Chillies","1 tablespoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","2 tablespoons Jaggery","12 Colocasia Leaves (Arbi)","3 tablespoons Coriander (Dhania) Seeds","1 tablespoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","Salt - as per taste"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,2311,9,2314,973,48], steps: ["To begin making the Pathrode Recipe, wash and soak the rice and dal in water for 3 to 6 hours.Wash the colocasia leaves,","This will help them cook fast and make them less itchy.Drain off the excess water from rice and grind all mentioned masa","Keep leaf upside down and smear a layer of masala on back side of leaf","Place the second leaf on top of the first leaf & smear masala","Repeat the process for 3 to 5 leaves.In one pathravadev roll there should be minimum 3 leaves","Now pathravade is ready for rolls","Firstly fold the sides of the leaf towards the centre and then roll along length of the leaves to make a roll.After it i","Once the rolls are done, steam cook these rolls 15 to 20 minutes ✅"] },
