"vellai_seedai_recipe_krishna_janmashtami_gokulasht": { title: "Vellai Seedai Recipe - Krishna Janmashtami | Gokulashtami Recipe", serves: "3", time: "720 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1/2 cup Jaggery","Sunflower Oil - for deep frying","1 cup Rice - washed","2 tablespoons White Urad Dal (Whole)","2 tablespoons Sesame seeds (Til seeds)","1/4 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","2 tablespoons Ghee","2 tablespoons Roasted Gram Dal (Pottukadalai)","2 tablespoons Water"], product_ids: [2307,2308,9,2314,4140,503,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Vellai Seedai Recipe, prepare all the ingredients and keep ready.Soak the rice for two hours and dra","Dry the rice in a kitchen towel overnight","Once dry, blend to make a fine powder.In a heavy bottomed pan on medium heat, roast the urad and bengal gram dals until ","Blend the Urad dal and chana dal into a fine powder and keep aside","In the same pan, toast the sesame seeds for a few seconds and then add the coconut and toast for another 30 seconds and ","Keep stirring until the jaggery dissolves in water and comes to a brisk boil for a few seconds","Into a large wide bowl; add the rice flour, urad chana dal flour, coconut sesame seed mixture, elaichi powder, and ghee.","Now grease your palms with ghee and and shape the dough to make small marble size balls ✅"] },
