"besan_atta_ki_roti_recipe_chickpea_flatbread": { title: "Besan & Atta Ki Roti Recipe (Chickpea Flatbread)", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["Ghee - or oil for cooking","1 Green Chilli - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1/4 teaspoon Ajwain (Carom seeds)","2 cups Gram flour (besan)","1 Onion - finely chopped","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - small bunch","1 cup Whole Wheat Flour","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1 teaspoon Salt"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,4140,973,4143,2300,476], steps: ["To begin making the Besan & Atta Ki Roti Recipe (Chickpea Flatbread), first get all the ingredients ready and keep aside","Add a little water at a time and knead to make a smooth dough","Drizzle a teaspoon of oil over the dough and knead for a couple of minutes until smooth and firm","Divide the besan roti dough into 10 portions.Preheat the Roti Tawa on medium heat","Roll each portion of the dough, but dusting in flour into a thin circle","The thickness of the besan ki roti will be based on how thin you can roll it","Once rolled, place the besan ki roti on the Roti Tawa and allow it to cook for a few seconds","Once you see air bubbles popping out, flip and turn ✅"] },
"instant_tindora_and_carrot_pickle_recipe": { title: "Instant Tindora And Carrot Pickle Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["2 cloves Garlic - finely minced","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1/8 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","15 Dry Red Chillies - (adjust)","1 Carrot (Gajjar)","2 Green Chillies - slit lengthwise","15 Tindora (Dondakaya/ Kovakkai) - (firm)","1/4 cup Sesame (Gingelly) Oil - (gingelly oil)","4 Curry leaves","1/4 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","1 teaspoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds"], product_ids: [929,930,2307,973,468,920,2300,2301], steps: ["To prepare Instant Tindora & Carrot Pickle Recipe, wash and trim the edges of the tindora/ tindli/ ivy gourd","Take care not to burn them, keep the flame simmer and roast the ingredients.Let the roasted ingredients cool well","Then, in a mixer-grinder, grind to a fine powder.Now to make the pickle, heat a kadai/pan, add gingelly oil (sesame oil)","Saute for a minute.Add hing to this and saute again for a minute.Add tindora (ivy gourd) and carrot, along with turmeric","Keep the flame in medium, and let the veggies sizzle for about 10-12 minutes","Keep stirring every couple of minutes, so that the veggies do not stick to the bottom or burn","Do not overcook the veggies.Add the ground masala powder and salt to the veggies","Mix well.Let this simmer for another 5 minutes for the masala to mingle well with veggies ✅"] },
