"zarda_pulav_recipe_rice_flavoured_with_nuts_and_sa": { title: "Zarda Pulav Recipe (Rice Flavoured With Nuts And Saffron)", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Basmati rice","1 Saffron strands - generous pinch","2 tablespoons Ghee - plus 1 teaspoon Ghee (Vegans can use coconut oil)","3/4 teaspoon Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)","2 Bay leaf (tej patta)","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","Whole cashews - chopped","Raisins - as required (for garnishing)","3 tablespoon Milk - coconut milk or almond milk","Pistachios - chopped","2 Black cardamom (Badi Elaichi)","Nutmeg powder - a pinch"], product_ids: [2307,2308,8,9,2314,4140,4141,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Zarda Pulav recipes, warm the milk in a saucepan, add saffron and keep it aside for an hour so that ","Once washed properly, soak it in required amount of water for about half an hour.Take 4 to 5 cups of water in a large sa","Allow the water to come to a boil.Add a teaspoon of ghee and then add rice and gently stir it for 15 seconds","Par boil the rice i.e","cook it till it is cooked approximately eighty percent","(just as one would cook for layered biryani).Drain and sieve excess water in a colander and remove the rice on a wide pl","Remove on an absorbent sheet.In the same pan add cloves, black cardamom, bay leaf, green cardamom and cinnamon stick","Allow the spices to become aromatic ✅"] },
