"tandoori_style_soya_chaap_curry_recipe": { title: "Tandoori Style Soya Chaap Curry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["Sunflower Oil - as required","1 Tablespoon Ginger Garlic Paste","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder","Salt - to taste","1 Red Bell pepper (Capsicum)","4 Green Chillies","1/4 teaspoon Kashmiri Red Chilli Powder","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - Fresh (chopped)","1/4 cup Cheese - grated","1 teaspoon Tandoori masala","1/2 teaspoon Red Chilli powder","1/2 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2314,973,4142,1840,4145,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Tandoori Style Soya Chaap Curry recipe, first remove the sticks from Soya chaap and dice them small ","Use your hands to rub the mixture on soya chaap","Let it marinate for 15 minutes.Meanwhile, take the red pepper and keep it directly on gas (fire) for roasting","Roast till it gets charred from all the sides","Let it cool down for few minutes","Use your hands to remove the burnt skin from the pepper","Grind the roasted pepper & green chillies together.Now take the marinated soya chaaps and add red pepper paste, whisked ","Give it a good stir so that soya chunks are properly coated ✅"] },
