"ridge_gourd_chutney_recipe_beerakaya_pachadi": { title: "Ridge Gourd Chutney Recipe (Beerakaya Pachadi)", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["3 Green Chillies","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","2 Ridge Gourd (Turai/ Peerkangai)","3 Dry Red Chillies","8 Curry leaves","1 teaspoon Tamarind - seedless","1 tablespoon Chana dal (Bengal Gram Dal)","1/2 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","Salt - as per taste","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 tablespoon Sunflower Oil"], product_ids: [929,2307,2308,2311,973,1844,503,920], steps: ["To begin making the Ridge Gourd Chutney recipe, wash & chop the ridge gourd into small pieces","You can opt to remove the skin if it is too flakey & thick.Heat oil in a heavy-bottomed pan","Add the chana dal & fry it till it changes colour","Remove it into a plate and let it cool.Now in the same pan, add the chopped ridge gourds, curry leaves, green chillies, ","Mix it well.Cover it & let it cook for 8-10 minutes till it loses all the water and becomes soft and mushy","Switch off the stove and leave it to cool.Now, in a separate pan add the mustard seeds, fenugreek seeds and dry red chil","Once done, add these to a grinder/mixer jar &Once done, add these to a grinder/mixer jar & grind to a fine powder","You can make this powder in an excess amount and store it ✅"] },
