"mangalorean_style_masala_pundi_recipe_steamed_rice": { title: "Mangalorean Style Masala Pundi Recipe - Steamed rice dumpling in Onion", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "☕ Beverage", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Dosa rice - washed and dried completely","1 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","4 tablespoon Fresh coconut","Salt - to taste","1 cup Tamarind Water","1/2 cup Fresh coconut - grated","1 Onion - chopped","2 cloves Garlic - chopped","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 tablespoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 tablespoon Salt","2 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Seeds"], product_ids: [929,930,2307,2308,2311,9,973,2300], steps: ["Steam the dumplings for about 20 minutes.We will move ahead to make the curry, heat a small skillet with a teaspoon of o","Add coriander seeds, fenugreek seeds and roast them for 10 seconds","Later add the dry red chillies, cumin seeds, urad dal and roast them well too for another 10 seconds.Take these roasted ","Add little water to grind it smoothly.Heat a kadai with oil, add the mustard seeds and splutter for few seconds and add ","Once that crackles add the chopped onions and garlic and saute till the onions becomes translucent.Add turmeric powder, ","Check for salt ✅"] },
"udupi_style_heerekai_bajji_recipe_ridge_gourd_frit": { title: "Udupi Style Heerekai Bajji Recipe-Ridge Gourd Fritters", serves: "3", time: "20 min", category: "🥟 Snack", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Red Chilli powder","1 Ridge Gourd (Turai/ Peerkangai) - skin peeled and cut into roundels","Salt - to taste","Sunflower Oil - for cooking","2 tablespoon Rice flour","1 cup Gram flour (besan)","1/2 teaspoon Baking soda","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)"], product_ids: [2307,2308,973,1844,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["We begin making the Udupi Style Heerekai Bajji Recipe, wash and peel the ridge gourd","Cut them into roundels and set aside","To make the bajji batterIn a mixing bowl, combine besan flour, rice flour, red chilli powder, turmeric powder, baking so","Mix well to a make a smooth batter.Heat a kuzhi paniyaram pan, and add a teaspoon of oil in each of the cavities","Dip the ridge gourd roundels in the batter completely and place it in the cavity","Cook it till it crisp on either side","Flip it over and continue to cook","Remove and drain it on an absorbent paper ✅"] },
"puffed_rice_upma_recipe_murmura_upma": { title: "Puffed Rice Upma Recipe - Murmura Upma", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["1 Ginger - grated","1/2 teaspoon Mustard seeds","6 cups Puffed rice","2 tablespoon Lemon juice","1 tablespoon Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - finely chopped","10 Curry leaves - roughly torn","1 Onion - finely chopped","2 Green Chillies - finely chopped","Salt - as needed","1/4 cup Raw Peanuts (Moongphali)","1 tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1/4 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,973,48,2300,503,920], steps: ["To begin making Puffed Rice Upma Recipe (Murmura Upma), place the puffed rice in a strainer and wash it under running wa","Alternatively, if you like the upma crunchy you can directly add the puffed rice without washing it","Heat a heavy bottomed pan or kadai with a tablespoon of oil on medium flame","Once the oil heats up, add mustard seeds and allow it to crackle","Add cumin seeds and peanuts and roast on medium heat until the raw peanuts get a roasted aroma and are crisp.Once the pe","Add peas, turmeric powder, tomatoes and cook for 5 minutes until the tomatoes are tender and soft","Stir in the Murmura (Puffed Rice), coriander leaves, lemon juice and stir everything together","Check the salt and spice, adjust to suit your taste and serve ✅"] },
"andhra_style_kandagadda_vepudu_recipe_yam_stir_fry": { title: "Andhra Style Kandagadda Vepudu Recipe - Yam Stir Fry Recipe", serves: "3", time: "40 min", category: "🥡 Indo-Chinese", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","2 tablespoon Red Chilli powder","2 sprig Curry leaves","1 inch Ginger - chopped","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 Green Chilli - chopped","4 cloves Garlic - chopped","250 grams Elephant yam (Suran/Senai/Ratalu) - cut into small florets","1 teaspoon Black pepper powder"], product_ids: [2307,973,920,473,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Andhra Style Kandagadda Vepudu Recipe, firstly we will pressure cook the chopped yam","Add the Yam in a pressure cooker with 1 cup water and salt","Close the lid and cook till the cooker releases 2 whistles.Switch off the heat and allow it to rest so that it releases ","Once the oil is hot, add mustard seeds and allow it to splutter for few seconds","Add the curry leaves and crackle them for 10 more seconds.Add the ginger and garlic, chopped green chilli and cooked yam","Add the spice powders also (red chilli powder, turmeric powder, pepper powder and salt) and mix everything well.Mix unti","Check for salt and serve","Serve the Andhra Style Kandagadda Vepudu along with Steamed Rice, Palak Tovve or Palak Dal Recipe and Palya for an every"] },
"whole_wheat_oatmeal_and_amaranth_fruitcake_cookie": { title: "Whole Wheat, Oatmeal and Amaranth Fruitcake Cookie Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 to 2 tablespoons Dark Chocolate Chips","1/2 teaspoon Baking soda - slightly heaped","1 Whole Eggs - beaten ( Mashed banana to replace egg)","1 cup Instant Oats (Oatmeal)","3/4 cup Dry Fruits - rum soaked","3/4 cup Sunflower Oil","1/2 cup Rajgira Flour (Amaranth Flour)","5 tablespoons Milk","1/2 cup Brown Sugar (Demerara Sugar) - adjustable","1/4 cup Walnuts - coarsley chopped","2 tablespoons Whole Wheat Flour","1 tablespoon Flax seed powder (flax meal)"], product_ids: [2314,4141,4148,27,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin the Whole Wheat, Oatmeal and Amaranth Fruitcake Cookie Recipe, preheat oven to 180 degree Celsius","Add it during the above step with the rest of the dry ingredients and mix well.) oil & milk together","Make a well in the center of the dry ingredients and pour in the egg mixture","Mix the mixture together well with either a fork or a whisk or a wooden spoon to make a soft but not sticky dough.Shape ","Transfer the biscuits to a preheated oven and bake for 10 -12 mins until golden","(oven times may vary)Remove from the oven and allow it to cool for 2-3 mins on the baking sheet.Transfer the cookies to ","Serve the Whole Wheat, Oatmeal and Amaranth Fruitcake Cookie cold or store in an airtight container to serve later.Notes","So don't worry if you don't achieve the usual cookie texture ✅"] },
"roasted_bell_pepper_quinoa_recipe": { title: "Roasted Bell Pepper Quinoa Recipe", serves: "3", time: "30 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Extra Virgin Olive Oil","1 Red Bell pepper (Capsicum) - finely chopped","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Lemon juice","4 cloves Garlic - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Rosemary","1 cup Quinoa","2 cups Water","1 Green Bell Pepper (Capsicum) - finely chopped","1 teaspoon Black pepper powder"], product_ids: [2307,460,48,1840,2300,2301,2302,2303], steps: ["To begin making the Roasted Bell Pepper Quinoa Recipe, wash the quinoa and set aside","In a pressure cooker, combine the quinoa with water, add 1 teaspoon olive oil and salt, mix well and close the pressure ","Pressure cook the quinoa for 4 whistles and turn off the heat","Allow the pressure to release naturally","In a skillet, heat oil on medium flame, add the garlic and saute until it turns into a light brown colour","To this add rosemary, finely chopped bell peppers, salt and cook on high heat for a couple of minutes until the bell pep","Stir in the quinoa to the roasted bell peppers, add freshly squeezed lemon juice and toss well ✅"] },
