"dry_fruit_burfi_recipe_with_gulkand": { title: "Dry Fruit Burfi Recipe With Gulkand", serves: "3", time: "70 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoons Gulkand","1 cup Dates - chopped","1 Edible Silver Foil/Leaf (Chandi Ka Vark) - optional","1/3 cup Walnuts","1/3 cup Cashew nuts","1 1/2 cups Dried Figs - chopped","1 tablespoon Ghee","1/3 cup Pistachios","1/3 cup Badam (Almond)","1/3 cup Raisins","1/4 teaspoon Nutmeg powder"], product_ids: [2307,8,4140,2300,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Dry Fruit Burfi With Gulkand Recipe, soak the chopped anjeer/dried figs in warm water for 15 minutes","Grind anjeer/figs along with the dates and raisins to smooth paste without adding any water","Keep it aside.Meanwhile finely chop almonds, cashewnuts, walnut and pista","Once you notice the burfi mixture comes away from the sides of the pan turn off the heat","Grease a tray with ghee and pour burfi mixture into the tray","Level it well with a spatula and allow mixture to cook completely and set itself into a firm burfi.Optionally add the si","Cut the Dry Fruit Burfi into desired shapes.Serve Dry Fruit Burfi With Gulkand as a festival dessert along with Jalebi a"] },
"kerala_style_prawns_shrimp_biryani_chemmeen_biryan": { title: "Kerala Style Prawns & Shrimp Biryani -Chemmeen Biryani Recipe", serves: "3", time: "220 min", category: "🍚 Rice", all_ingredients: ["1/4 cup Mint Leaves (Pudina) - finely chopped","1 Onion - finely sliced","1 Fresh coconut - handful","1/2 tablespoon Ginger - paste","1 Salt - to taste","1 tablespoon Ginger Garlic Paste","1/2 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","6 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 Raisins - handful","3-4 tablespoons Lemon juice","Salt - to taste","1 teaspoon Garam masala powder"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,2308,8,9,2314,4140], steps: ["Start making Kerala Style Prawns & Shrimp Biryani (Chemmeen Biryani Recipe) by mixing prawns with ingredients mentioned ","Combine well and cook for another 2 to 3 minutes till the mixture thickens slightly","Cover the pressure cooker with lid without weight.Cook on a high flame till a strong steam comes through","Remove them from the pan and fry the onions till golden brown.Drain any excess ghee on a paper towel.Layering The Biryan","Next add a layer of rice as the second layer","Repeat layers till the masala and rice is used up completely","The top most layer of the biriyani must be the rice","Drizzle a little ghee between each layer ✅"] },
"keema_kaleji_recipe_mutton_liver_mince": { title: "Keema Kaleji Recipe- Mutton Liver Mince", serves: "3", time: "55 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["6 Green Chillies","1/2 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt) - sour","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - Fresh for garnish (chopped)","5 Cloves (Laung)","2 Black cardamom (Badi Elaichi)","2-1/2 tablespoon Garlic - minced","1 teaspoon Mace (Javitri)","Salt - to taste","400 grams Mutton - Kaleji / Liver","4 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds - green","4 Dry Red Chillies","1-1/2 tablespoon Red Chilli powder"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,2314,973,4142,48,946], steps: ["Now add chopped onions and saute till golden","Add minced ginger and garlic and fry till raw smell goes off","Meanwhile, take curd in a bowl and whisk to break lumps and keep aside","When the ginger garlic and onion mix is golden, add washed keema and kaleji together and mix well.Keep the flames high n","Add in the whisked curd and mix thoroughly till curd starts leaving water.Add some turmeric powder and salt and give a q","Adjust oil and salt if required and fry till the keema kaleji is completely done","Drizzle some lemon juice all over and turn off the gas","Garnish with some freshly chopped coriander and serve hot Serve Keema Kaleji along with Tawa Parathas, Mutton Biryani an"] },
