"mughlai_style_chicken_changezi_recipe": { title: "Mughlai Style Chicken Changezi Recipe", serves: "3", time: "60 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["2 tablespoon Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","1 tablespoon Coriander Powder (Dhania)","3/4 teaspoon Cumin powder (Jeera)","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 teaspoon Ginger Garlic Paste","1 cup Homemade tomato puree","Salt - to taste","1-1/2 teaspoon Kashmiri Red Chilli Powder","750 grams Chicken - cleaned","4 tablespoons Sunflower Oil","1 tablespoon Ginger - finely chopped","1/2 teaspoon Kasuri Methi (Dried Fenugreek Leaves)"], product_ids: [545,930,929,2307,2314,973,4141,4142], steps: ["To begin making the Chicken Changezi recipe, pat dry the chicken well after cleaning and prick it with a fork","Burn a small piece of charcoal on the direct flame.Place your chicken in a dish, once it is cooked","In the middle place a katori","Put the blazing charcoal in that katori and pour ghee over it","Cover and let it rest till all the smoke is infused in the chicken","This will give you a smoky flavor to chicken","Now, for the gravy, heat oil in a heavy bottomed pan","Add the ginger garlic and cook for about 30 seconds or till the raw smell disappears.Add tomato puree and masala gravy o"] },
