"homemade_butter_naan_recipe_soft_yogurt_bread": { title: "Homemade Butter Naan Recipe - Soft Yogurt Bread", serves: "3", time: "90 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["1 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","1 tablespoon Sugar","1 tablespoon Butter - softened","1/2 cup Butter (unsalted) - softened","1-1/2 teaspoons Salt","2 teaspoons Chaat Masala Powder","3 cups All Purpose Flour (Maida)","2 teaspoons Active dry yeast","3 tablespoons Lukewarm Water"], product_ids: [2307,2314,4142,4144,2300,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Butter Naan recipe, in a large bowl add the 3 cups of flour and butter","With your hands, blend the butter into the flour until it forms coarse crumbs","You can do this in a blender as well, but the dough when worked with hands gives a better texture to the dough.Stir toge","Now make a well in the center of the flour mixture and add the yogurt, salt and yeast mixture.Knead into the flour and u","Add a little more water if required to bring the dough together","The dough will be wet and sticky","Wipe your hands clean and oil them","Now knead the naan dough with the oiled hands until smooth , for about 10 minutes; oil your hands more if the dough is s"] },
"radish_leaves_pachadi_recipe": { title: "Radish Leaves Pachadi Recipe", serves: "3", time: "35 min", category: "🍛 South Indian", all_ingredients: ["1 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)","2 Green Chillies - split","Salt - to taste","10 Dry Red Chillies - (adjust)","2 Tablespoon Sunflower Oil","1 teaspoon Methi Seeds (Fenugreek Seeds)","2 inch Tamarind","1 Tablespoon White Urad Dal (Split)","3 cloves Garlic","1 Tablespoon Mustard seeds","1 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","1 Tomato - chopped"], product_ids: [545,929,2307,2308,2311,973,463,503], steps: ["To prepare Radish Leaves Pachadi Recipe, prep up with all the ingredients required.Heat oil in a pan, add half of mustar","When they start spluttering, add hing.Add in green chillies, red chillies, and fry for a few seconds.Add chopped tomatoe","By now the above radish leaves and tomato mixture might have cooled","Add them to a blender jar, add salt, turmeric powder, and tamarind ✅"] },
