"maharashtrian_kadhi_recipe": { title: "Maharashtrian Kadhi Recipe", serves: "3", time: "35 min", category: "🫘 Dal", all_ingredients: ["1 tablespoon Sugar","1 sprig Coriander (Dhania) Leaves - chopped","1 teaspoon Cumin seeds (Jeera)","1 inch Ginger - grated","1 teaspoon Mustard seeds","1 Green Chilli - chopped","4 tablespoon Gram flour (besan)","1 cup Hung Curd (Greek Yogurt)","1 sprig Curry leaves - chopped","1 pinch Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [930,2307,2308,2314,973,4142,920,2300], steps: ["To begin making the Maharashtrian Kadhi Recipe, first mix the yogurt and besan in a bowl","Keep whisking till it thickens.Add salt and sugar and adjust it according to your taste","Switch off the heat.Once the kadhi is ready, garnish the kadhi with some chopped fresh coriander leaves.Serve the Mahara"] },
"lauki_yakhni_recipe_bottle_gourd_in_yogurt_gravy": { title: "Lauki Yakhni Recipe - Bottle Gourd In Yogurt Gravy", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🍛 North Indian", all_ingredients: ["Salt - as required","1 cup Curd (Dahi / Yogurt)","1/2 teaspoon Dry ginger powder","1 inch Cinnamon Stick (Dalchini)","1 teaspoon Fennel Powder","3-4 Cloves (Laung)","1 1/2 tablespoon Mustard oil","1/2 teaspoon Ajwain (Carom seeds)","2-3 Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","1 Bottle gourd (lauki)","1/4 teaspoon Asafoetida (hing)"], product_ids: [2307,2308,2314,4142,462,2300,2301,2302], steps: ["To begin with the Lauki Yakhini Recipe, let's first cut lauki (bottle gourd) into small cubes.Heat half a tablespoon oil","place the lauki in the tawa and let them fry until they are tender and brown","Once done keep them aside","Add some more oil in the same pan and add cloves, cinnamon stick, carom seeds and saute until nice aroma comes out of it","Add required amount of salt and simmer the curry for a minute.Taste the gravy and if you feel it needs some more salt ad","Switch off the flame and garnish with coriander leaves.Serve Lauki Yakhni Recipe along with Aamras and Tawa Paratha for ","You can also pack this for your Lunch Box ✅"] },
"twice_baked_potatoes_recipe": { title: "Twice Baked Potatoes Recipe", serves: "3", time: "50 min", category: "🌍 World Cuisine", all_ingredients: ["1 Green Chilli - finely chopped","Salt and Pepper - as required","1/2 teaspoon Turmeric powder (Haldi)","pinch Coriander Powder (Dhania)","1 tablespoon Sour cream","1/2 teaspoon Amchur (Dry Mango Powder)","1 tablespoon All Purpose Flour (Maida)","pinch Kashmiri Red Chilli Powder","1-2 teaspoons Extra Virgin Olive Oil","pinch Cumin powder (Jeera)","1/3 cup Mozzarella cheese - grated","4 Potatoes (Aloo) - (2 if large) scrubbed clean"], product_ids: [1,930,2307,973,4141,4142,4144,4145], steps: ["To begin making the Twice Baked Potatoes first preheat the oven to 180 degrees C.Rub the cleaned potatoes with some oil ","Take a square of aluminium foil and wrap each potato tightly inside it.When the oven is hot enough, place the covered po","When done, remove them from the oven and allow them to cool slightly.Open the potatoes up and halve them","Scoop the flesh out leaving just enough inside so the potato forms a firm shell outside","Collect the baked potato in a bowl and set aside till later use.Meanwhile, in a skillet heat 1/2 tablespoon butter over ","Add the onions, green chilli, salt and pepper and cook down till the onions are nicely browned","This might take 7-8 minutes.Next, add the garlic, ginger and cook until fragrant","Stir in the peas and toss to coat well ✅"] },
