"makki_ki_roti_recipe_a_classic_north_indian_corn_r": { title: "Makki Ki Roti Recipe - A Classic North Indian Corn Roti", serves: "4", time: "55 min", category: "🥤 Smoothie", all_ingredients: ["Makki Ka Atta (Yellow Corn Meal Flour)","Ajwain (Carom seeds)","Salt","Lukewarm Water","White Butter","Jaggery","Green Chillies","Ginger","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves"], product_ids: [930,2307,2314,973,4144,1842,2302], steps: ["To begin making the Makki Ki Roti, combine all the ingredients except the ghee/butter in a mixing bowl","Add a little warm water at a time and make a soft dough. It is important to knead well for 3 to 4 minutes to get the dou","Divide the makki ki roti dough into large lemon size portions, cover the dough and keep aside","Preheat an iron skillet; place a wet muslin cloth on the working surface; wet the palms of your hands and place a dough ","Invert the muslin cloth over the preheated skillet and place the rolled out makki roti on skillet. Cook the roti on medi","Once you notice lighter brown spots, flip the Makki ki Roti over direct flame until it is completely cooked through","Once done, smear some white butter on the Makki Roti and serve hot","Serve the Makki Ki Roti along with ✅"] },
