"mussels_in_asian_style_recipe": { title: "Mussels In Asian Style Recipe", serves: "4", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["Mussels","Sunflower Oil","Red Chilli Paste","Onion powder","Garlic","Ginger","Apple cider vinegar","Garlic powder","Turmeric powder (Haldi)","Mint Leaves (Pudina)","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves","Water"], product_ids: [0,930,2307,973,946,476,2301], steps: ["To begin making the Mussels In Asian Style, wash mussels well in cold water for 3 to 4 times. Discard any beards if pres","Mine are already slightly opened, because I had bought them the previous day and had chilled them in the freezer, but if","While cooking they will open up. Heat oil in a saucepan and once the oil is heated, saute minced ginger, garlic on mediu","Add 2 tablespoons of red chili paste, onion powder and saute for few more seconds. Add water and mussels","Mix well. Cover and cook on medium high heat for about 10 minutes","After 10 minutes, the mussels will open up. Discard any unopened ones","Keep stirring in between. Add garlic powder, 1 tablespoon red chili paste, vinegar, mint and coriander leaves","Mix, cover and simmer for another 5 minutes on medium heat. Remove cover and add turmeric powder. This helps to eliminat"] },
