"soya_chunks_sabzi": { title: "Soya Chunks Sabzi", serves: "4", time: "30 min", category: "🍛 Curry", all_ingredients: ["Soy Chunks (Nuggets)","Hot water","Onion","Garlic","Ginger","Tomatoes","Red Chilli powder","Chaat Masala Powder","Salt","Lemon juice","Coriander (Dhania) Leaves"], product_ids: [545,930,2307,973,48,476,2302], steps: ["Start preparing Soya Chunks Sabzi Recipe by soaking soya chunks in hot water and salt for 15 minutes","Meanwhile, chop all the veggies and heat a","with oil and add chopped onions and cook for a couple of minutes until the onions turn translucent","Add sliced garlic, add Julian sliced ginger. Sauté for 10-15 seconds","Add slit green chilies. Add finely chopped tomatoes","Once tomatoes appear cooked, add red chili powder as per your taste","Add garam masala and chaat masala","Drain all the water from soya chunks and squeeze them properly ✅"] },
"doodhi_halwa_recipe_bottle_gourd_halwa": { title: "Doodhi Halwa Recipe (Bottle Gourd Halwa)", serves: "4", time: "65 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["Bottle gourd (lauki)","Milk","Sugar","Cashew nuts","Cardamom Powder (Elaichi)"], product_ids: [2314,2307,4141,462], steps: ["To begin the preparation of Doodhi Halwa, in a deep heavy bottom pan heat 3/4th ghee","Add grated bottle gourd and saute it for a couple of minutes","Add milk to this and cook on a low flame till all the milk evaporates and the doodhi is cooked with no raw smell left","Add sugar and cook till the sugar melts and is completely soaked by the doodhi","Keep mixing it to avoid it from sticking to the bottom","Once the sugar is completely soaked up, increase the flame and cook it for a minute and let the halwa caramelize slightl","In a small pan, heat the remaining ghee and add the cashews and raisins, let them turn gold","Pour the tempering over the halwa and give it a good mix ✅"] },
"rajasthani_hare_chane_ka_halwa_recipe_choliya_halw": { title: "Rajasthani Hare Chane Ka Halwa Recipe (Choliya Halwa)", serves: "4", time: "50 min", category: "🍮 Dessert", all_ingredients: ["Fresh green chickpeas","Sugar","Cardamom (Elaichi) Pods/Seeds","Pistachios","Raisins"], product_ids: [8,2314,2307,503], steps: ["To begin making the Rajasthani Hare Chane Ka Halwa recipe, heat a heavy bottom kadai/pan with ghee","Add the ground choliya mixture and keep stirring over low flame for 7-8 minutes or till the time they are cooked","Now add sugar and cardamom powder and continue to keep stirring till the time all the extra moisture is absorbed and the","Switch off. Heat ghee in a small pan and add the dry fruits for garnish and fry till fragrant and pour it over the halwa","Delicious Rajasthani Choliya Halwa is ready to be served. Serve Rajasthani Hare Chane Ka Halwa as a dessert after your m"] },
